hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6601","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no soul that dies having good with Allah, mighty and majestic, that would be pleased to return to the world though it had the world with what is in it — except the martyr; because of what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom, he would be pleased to return and be killed another time. And this hadith — Khalid and Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated it and did not raise it; and it is well known from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6602","And with his chain, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour shall not come until there remains on the earth no one saying: Allah, Allah."
"6603","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: Return your clarified butter to its skin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting. Then he stood to a side of the house and prayed a non-obligatory prayer, and supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Umm Sulaym said: I have a special little one. He said: What is she? She said: Your servant Anas. Then he left no good of the Hereafter or this world but that he supplicated for me with it. Then he said: Grant him wealth and children and bless him — I reckon he said: therein. He said: I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar. He said: And my daughter informed me that I had buried, by the time al-Hajjaj came to Basra, one hundred and twenty-odd."
"6604","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a walled garden of the walls of Madinah belonging to Banu al-Najjar, and heard a sound from a grave. He said: When was this one buried? They said: In the Jahiliyyah. That pleased him, and he said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have supplicated Allah, blessed and exalted, to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"6605","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It does not harm you — or a word like it — to marvel at anyone, or at the deed of anyone, until you see with what he is sealed. For a man works for a period of time the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered Paradise; then he works with the deed of the people of the Fire. And a servant works for a period of his life with the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered the Fire; then he works with the deed of the people of Paradise."
"6606","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting of Allah, mighty and majestic, Allah loves his meeting; and whoever hates the meeting of Allah, mighty and majestic, Allah hates his meeting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us hate death. He said: That is not the hatred of death; rather the believer, when he is dying, the bearer of glad tidings from Allah, mighty and majestic, comes to him, and nothing is more beloved to him than the meeting of Allah, mighty and majestic — so Allah loves his meeting and he loves the meeting of Allah, blessed and exalted. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except Humayd."
"6607","And with his chain, he said: Anas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave of the spoils of Khaybar to al-Aqra' ibn Habis one hundred camels and to Uyaynah ibn Badr one hundred camels. Some people of the Ansar said: He gives our spoils to a people whose swords drip with our blood — or: whose blood drips from our swords! When the Ansar gathered to him, he said: Is there among you any other than you? They said: No, except the son of our sister. He said: The son of the sister of a people is of them. Then he said: Are you not pleased, O company of the Ansar, that the people go with the world — or he said: with the camels and sheep — and you go with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your homes? They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Had the people taken a valley and the Ansar taken a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner garment and my receptacle; and were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar."
"6608","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three — whoever has them finds through them the sweetness of faith: one to whom Allah and His Messenger are more beloved than all besides them; one who loves a person loving him only for Allah; and one who hates to return to disbelief as he hates to be cast into the Fire."
"6609","And Ibn Muthanna narrated it to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Three — whoever has them... And he did not raise it."
"6610","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, who said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a river whose banks were tents of pearl. I struck my hand to the course of its water, and there I was with strongly fragrant musk. I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you."
"6611","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording... except that he said: which He has given you."
"6612","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come to you peoples whose hearts are more tender than yours. Then the Ash'aris came, among them Abu Musa."
"6613","And with his chain, he said: Abu Talhah was before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his head looking at the trace of the place of his arrows. He said: And Abu Talhah would stretch himself, saying: O Messenger of Allah, my soul for your soul as ransom — or he said: my throat before your throat."
"6614","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What if Allah withholds the fruit — with what do you consume the wealth of your brother?"
"6615","And with his chain, he said: The prayer was established, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had something between him and his wives, holding some of them back from others. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, came and said: Throw dust in their faces and go out to the prayer."
"6616","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting — I reckon he said: in his house — when a man looked in upon him, so he motioned toward him with a barbed arrowhead he had with him, and the man drew back."
"6617","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that he was asked about the punishment of the grave, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and decrepitude, cowardice and miserliness, the trial of the Dajjal and the punishment of the grave."
"6618","Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the supper is placed and the prayer is established, begin with the supper. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except al-Mu'tamir."
"6619","al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that a man granted a life-grant to a man, and he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: It is for his heirs — or as he said. And this hadith — we heard it only from al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah, and we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this angle."
"6620","al-Husayn ibn Abi Kabshah narrated to us; Attab ibn Harb narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"6621","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire, even with half a date. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad, from Humayd, from Anas, except Muhammad ibn al-Fadl."
"6622","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us; Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Abu Talhah wanted to divorce Umm Sulaym, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The divorce of Umm Sulaym is a grave sin. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Ali ibn Asim."
"6623","Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Sharik."
"6624","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remorse is repentance. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Yahya ibn Ayyub; and we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this angle. And this Amr ibn Malik narrated hadiths from Ibn Wahb and from al-Walid, mentioning that he heard them in the Hijaz; and the companions of hadith denied that these narrated them except in Egypt and Sham."
"6625","al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us; Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brown in complexion."
"6626","And Muhammad ibn Muthanna narrated it to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither tall nor short; and when he walked he leaned forward; and he was brown in complexion. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Khalid and Abd al-Wahhab."
"6627","Ali ibn Harb narrated to us; al-Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Persist with: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except from this angle."
"6628","Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us; Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A house in the heights of Paradise, a house in the courtyard of Paradise, and a house in the middle of Paradise — for one who abandons lying even while joking, for one who abandons disputation even while right, and for one whose character is good."
"6629","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us; Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out on a journey and returned and drew near Madinah, would hasten toward it."
"6630","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Kirmani narrated to us; Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us; al-Khazraj ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khaybar on halves, or on thirds. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it except al-Khazraj."
"6631","al-Husayn ibn Abi Kabshah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, none of us would prostrate until we saw him prostrate. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn al-Fadl; and al-Mu'tamir narrated it from his father, from a man, from Anas."
"6632","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The wife of Thabit ibn Shammas — and he is Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas — came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke words as though she disliked him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you return his garden to him? She said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Thabit: Take that from her — I reckon he said: and divorce her. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Abu Ja'far al-Razi; and Hammad ibn Salamah differed from him, saying: From Humayd, from Abu al-Khalil, as an unsourced narration."
"6633","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Ubayd ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman has two husbands in the world — meaning one husband after a husband — and they enter Paradise; for which of them shall she be? He said: For the better of them in character. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Sinan ibn Harun, a man of the people of Kufa, there is no harm in him."
"6634","Mufarrij ibn Shuja' ibn Ubaydillah al-Dhuhli narrated to us; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Abdah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, who said: When Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, he began tapping his front teeth with a rod, saying: He was — I reckon he said: handsome. So I said: By Allah, I shall grieve you; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing where your rod falls. He said: So he recoiled. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Yusuf ibn Abdah, and he is a man of the people of Basra, well known, there is no harm in him."
"6635","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Ayyub: Shall I not guide you to a trade? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Strive in reconciliation between people when they are corrupted, and bring them together when they are distant. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this angle; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Abdullah ibn Umar, nor anyone who narrated it from him except Abd al-Rahman his son. And Abd al-Rahman is lenient in hadith, and he narrated hadiths upon which he was not followed."
"6636","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: Anas ibn al-Nadr was absent from the fighting of Badr, so he said: I was absent from the first fighting which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought against the polytheists? If Allah, blessed and exalted, lets me witness fighting alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah, blessed and exalted, shall see how I act. When the day of Uhud came and the Muslims were uncovered, he said: O Allah, I disavow to You what these have brought — meaning the polytheists — and I apologize to You for what these have done — meaning the Muslims. Then he went forth with his sword, and Sa'd ibn Mu'adh met him and said: Where to, O Sa'd? By Allah, I smell it before Uhud. He said: So he went and fought. Anas said: We found upon him eighty-odd — between a sword strike, a spear thrust and an arrow shot — and they mutilated him. He said: We recognized him only by his fingertip. He said: And this verse was revealed: (Among the believers are men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah)."
"6637","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, upon it a thick growth; between his eyes is written: k f r."
"6638","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us; Abu Asim al-Abbadani narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation shall enter Paradise, with each one of the seventy, seventy thousand. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except Abu Asim al-Abbadani."
"6639","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: There was no person more beloved to them than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); yet when they saw him they would not stand for him, because of his dislike of that."
"6640","And with his chain, he said: The people of Yemen came, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, more tender in hearts than you; and he is the first who came with handshaking."
"6641","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for the prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: Stand close together, stand close together; I see you from behind my back."
"6642","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us; Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine watermelon with fresh dates. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"6643","al-Qasim ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us; Yazid ibn Mihran narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, indeed strengthens the religion with peoples who have no share."
"6644","Yahya ibn Zakariyya informed us; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abu al-Anbas, from Abu al-Adabbas, from Abu Marzuq, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out leaning upon a staff, and we stood. He said: Do not stand as the non-Arabs stand, magnifying one another. It was as though we wished him to supplicate for us, so he said: O Allah, forgive us and have mercy upon us and be pleased with us, and accept from us, and admit us into Paradise and save us from the Fire, and set right for us all our affair. It was as though we wished him to add for us, so he said: I have gathered the matter for you."
"6645","And al-Abbas ibn Ja'far al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Yazid ibn Mihran narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by afflicted people and said: Did these not ask Allah for well-being? And these two hadiths — we do not know anyone who narrated them from Humayd except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"6646","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth, except by its right; and their reckoning is upon Allah, blessed and exalted."
"6647","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Umm Sulaym had a son called Abu Umayr, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes jest with him. One day he entered and found him grieved, and said: What is the matter with Abu Umayr? They said: His little bird with which he used to play has died. So he kept saying: O Abu Umayr, what has the little bird done?"
"6648","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan Abu Hammam narrated to us; Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin. Thus Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated it from Yunus; and others besides Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated it from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas."
"6649","Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Isa ibn Khalaf narrated to us; Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity repels an evil death. Anas is alone in it; and this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yunus except Abdullah ibn Isa, and we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this angle."
"6650","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us; Abu Khuzaymah narrated to us; Malik ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, indeed strengthens this religion with men who have no share. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Malik ibn Dinar; and this Abu Khuzaymah is a Basran, Habban narrated from him; and Ibn Nabhan narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Dinar with this chain."
"6651","Sulayman al-Taymi narrated from Anas: Najih ibn Ibrahim al-Kufi narrated to us; Dirar ibn Surad Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard my father narrating from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ali shall settle my debt. And this hadith is rejected."
"6652","al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Uruzzi and Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, both saying: Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it. Recite if you wish: (And extended shade). And this hadith — Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated it from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas; and we do not know anyone who said ""from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas"" except Abu Attab, from Sa'id."
"6653","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sahib al-Sabiri narrated to us; Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drinker and ordered him flogged; so he was flogged with palm stalks and sandals. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas; and I reckon Shababah is the one who erred in it."
"6654","And Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us; Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: Ali proposed to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... And he mentioned the hadith. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except al-Hasan ibn Hammad; and it was narrated from Anas from another angle, narrated by Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani, from his father, from Anas."
"6655","Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qurdusi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of youths, whoever of you has means, let him marry; and whoever does not, upon him is fasting — I reckon he said: for it is a restraint for him. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Baqiyyah; and others besides Baqiyyah narrated it from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from a man of the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him."
"6656","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out in the illness in which he died, leaning upon Usama, wrapped in a cotton garment, and prayed with the people. And we do not know that Habib narrated from al-Hasan, from Anas, except this hadith; nor did anyone narrate it from him except Hammad ibn Salamah. Anas is alone in it."
"6657","Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i narrated to us, both saying: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, who said: Abu Ziyad used to deny the Hawd, so it was said to him: Anas ibn Malik narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the Hawd. So he sent to Anas and asked him? Anas said: I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I have a Hawd from such-and-such to such-and-such."
"6658","Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Husayn ibn Kurdi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it."
"6659","He said: And Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us; Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know that Awf transmitted from al-Hasan, from Anas, except this hadith; nor did anyone narrate it from him connected except Hammad ibn Mas'adah; and we heard it only from Ahmad ibn Abdillah."
"6660","al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us; Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram, he and his companions, for Hajj and Umrah. When they arrived in Makkah, they circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to exit ihram, but they were awed by that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exit ihram; had the sacrificial animal not been with me, I would have exited ihram. So they exited ihram until they became lawful even to women. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik."
"6661","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us; Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and he mentioned the Hawd — saying: There are seen in it pitchers more numerous than the stars of the sky."
"6662","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer between graves. And this hadith — others besides Hafs narrated it from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without mentioning Anas; none mentioned Anas except Hafs. And Anas is alone in this hadith."
"6663","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi al-Kufi narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us; al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves, and for him is what he earned. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"6664","Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would open the recitation with (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds), and he was the lightest of people in prayer while complete. And this hadith — others besides Ash'ath narrated near to it; and Ash'ath is more beloved to me than any who narrated this hadith from al-Hasan, from Anas, besides him. And Anas is alone in it."
"6665","Harun ibn Sufyan al-Mustamli narrated to us; Mansur ibn Ikrimah narrated to us; Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan — and I think it is from Anas — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is white clothing; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Mansur ibn Ikrimah; and Mansur, there is no harm in him, a man of the people of Basra who moved to Wasit and resided there until he died."
"6666","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Adiyy narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan — and I think it is from Anas — raised, who said: This son of mine is a chief — meaning al-Hasan. He said: And he used to resemble him — or something like this."
"6667","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: Wine was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and their drink that day was only unripe dates and ripe dates."
"6668","Harun ibn Sufyan and Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in good as long as he does not hasten. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does he hasten? He said: He says: I have supplicated my Lord, but He has not answered me. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except al-Rabi' ibn Subayh; nor did anyone narrate it from al-Rabi' except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim. And Muhammad ibn al-Qasim is a Kufan; he was a man of sunnah; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated a hadith from him. And he is not strong; his hadith was tolerated. And Anas is alone in it."
"6669","Harun ibn Sufyan and Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: Bilal called the adhan before dawn, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to return and say: Indeed the servant slept. So Bilal ascended, saying: Would that Bilal were bereaved by his mother, and he became wet from the sprinkling of the blood of his forehead. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim; and our mention of him has preceded. Anas is alone in it."
"6670","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Dinar narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, they long for their brothers. So the couch of this one comes until it faces the couch of this one, and they converse; this one reclines and this one reclines, and they converse about what they were in the world. One of them says to his companion: O so-and-so, do you know on which day Allah forgave us — on the day we were in such-and-such place, and we supplicated Allah and He forgave us. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain from this angle; and Anas is alone in it."
"6671","6669 - Isa ibn Musa al-Shami narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on the day of Friday, then with it, and blessed is it; and whoever takes a full bath, then the bath is better. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas; more than one narrated it from him. And Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr combined in this hadith from al-Rabi', from al-Hasan and Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas; so a group of the people of hadith took it to mean that it is from al-Hasan also, from Anas. And I think that al-Rabi' only mentioned it from al-Hasan as mursal, and from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas; then since he did not separate it, they made it as if it is from al-Hasan, from Anas, and from Yazid, from Anas."
"6672","Imran al-Ammi from al-Hasan from him. 6670 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Imran al-Ammi, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will continue to intercede and my intercession will be accepted - or he said: my Lord will grant me intercession - until I say: O my Lord, You have granted me intercession regarding whoever said: There is no god but Allah? Then it will be said: O Muhammad, this is not for you nor for anyone; this is for Me. By My might and My mercy, I will not leave anyone in the Fire who says: There is no god but Allah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Imran; and none narrated it from Imran except Hammad ibn Mas'adah."
"6673","Ayyub ibn Abdillah from al-Hasan from him. 6671 - Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan narrated to us; Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us; Ayyub ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that it was said to him: Describe for us the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he called for a basin and performed ablution three times three times, and he ran his fingers through his beard, and said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Ayyub ibn Abdillah; and he is a man from the people of Basra; we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Mu'alla ibn Asad; and none narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6674","Umar ibn Nabhan from al-Hasan from him. 6672 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us; Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Abdillah, from Umar ibn Nabhan, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the house in which the Qur'an is recited, its goodness increases; and the house in which the Qur'an is not recited, its goodness decreases. Anas alone narrated it."
"6675","Mubarak ibn Fadalah from al-Hasan from him. 6673 - Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to me; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, Fatimah, may Allah have mercy on her, said: O the distress of my father's distress! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be no distress upon your father after today. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Mus'ab; and we heard it only from Abu Kurayb, from Mus'ab; Anas alone narrated it."
"6676","6674 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah when we came to Khaybar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed when we descend into the courtyard of a people, then evil is the morning of those who are warned."
"6677","6675 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, with the like of it; and he added in it: And a Jewish woman gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted sheep. Then when he extended his hand to eat, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed a limb of it informs me that it is poisoned. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refrained, and those with him refrained. So he sent for the Jewish woman and said: What carried you to spoil it after you had prepared it well? She said: I wanted to know: if you are a prophet, then you will know that; and if you are not a prophet, I will relieve the people of you. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Yazid, from Mubarak; Anas alone narrated it."
"6678","6676 - Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning against a palm trunk before he took the pulpit. Then when he took the pulpit, the trunk moaned. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and embraced it, and it calmed down. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Mubarak and Salim al-Khayyat."
"6679","6677 - Abdah ibn Abdillah al-Qasmali narrated to us; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim - or Ibrahim ibn Isma'il - stood up to al-Hasan and said: O Abu Sa'id, we hear from you hadiths that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so cite their chains for us. So he said: Ask about whatever occurs to you. So he said: The hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the establishment of the Hour. So he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Jabir ibn Abdillah narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Abdullah ibn Qudamah - and he was a truthful man - narrated to me, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then they stood up and said: We were almost overcome over this shaykh."
"6680","6678 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Adami narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ammar al-Tahi narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the caller to prayer, then say as he says. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this angle; and none narrated it from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Hafs ibn Ammar al-Tahi; and he was not followed in it; and he was a Basran who says: Tahiyah is very strange."
"6681","6679 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man who had become like a chick - meaning from severe pain - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him: Did you used to supplicate your Lord for something? He said: I used to say: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. So he said: Why did you not say - or why do you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us - or protect me - from the punishment of the Fire? He said: So the man said it, and he recovered. This hadith, this is its wording, or its meaning. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Abd al-Samad; and we heard it only from his son, from him; Anas alone narrated it."
"6682","6680 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Umar ibn Sahl narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne certainly shook for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Umar ibn Sahl; and Umar ibn Sahl is a Basran, there is no harm in him; he moved from Basra to Makkah and died there; and it is a strange hadith."
"6683","6681 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas."
"6684","6682 - And Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the souls are exhausted and the land is barren - or he said: the land has suffered drought - so ask Allah for rain for us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, give us rain. He said: And we did not see in the sky any cloud fragment. He said: Then the clouds gathered and they were rained upon until the like of it. Then that man - or another - stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, the houses have collapsed and the roads are cut off, so supplicate Allah to lift it from us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, around us, and not upon us. He said: Then the sky cleared over Madinah; so it would rain around it, and we would not be rained upon. And this hadith, this is its wording, or close to it. And we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Mubarak; and Thabit and Qatadah and Yahya narrated it."
"6685","6683 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us; Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Mubarak; and none narrated it from Mubarak except Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar; and Dawud was not a memorizer; and a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"6686","6684 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon a mat that had left marks on his side. So the eyes of Umar shed tears. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you weep, O Umar? He said: I remembered Kisra and Qaysar. He said: Are you not pleased that the world be for them and the Hereafter for us? This is its wording, or close to it."
"6687","6685 - Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Awf wrote to me, informing me that al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to him, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That three men entered a cave ... Then he mentioned the hadith in full. And none narrated this hadith from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except al-Haytham ibn Jamil; and everyone who narrated it from al-Haytham other than Muhammad ibn Awf has been spoken about and accused."
"6688","6686 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: When the Muslims and the polytheists met on the day of the conquest of Makkah ... And he mentioned the hadith."
"6689","6687 - Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from that which fire has touched. This is how Mubarak said: from al-Hasan, from Anas. And Matar said: from al-Hasan, from Anas, from Abu Talhah. And Ash'ath said: from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah."
"6690","Salim al-Khayyat from al-Hasan from him. 6688 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Salim al-Khayyat narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I never touched silk nor anything else softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and I never smelled musk nor amber more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Salim al-Khayyat; Anas alone narrated it."
"6691","6689 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Salim al-Khayyat, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accept from the doers of good among the Ansar and overlook their evildoers. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Salim."
"6692","6690 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hayyaj narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Salim al-Khayyat narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar used to begin the recitation with: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"6693","6691 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us; Ubaydullah narrated to us; Salim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I used to pour for my uncles a drink of unripe and ripe dates, until the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: That wine has been made unlawful. He said: So we poured it out. And in it is speech which we shortened, and we mentioned .... And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Salim except Ubaydullah ibn Musa."
"6694","Salih al-Murri from al-Hasan from him. 6692 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Sari, a Basran, narrated to us; Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that a beggar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave him a date. So he said: A prophet gives a date! And he left. Then another came and asked. So he sent, and a date was brought, and he gave him a date. So he said: A date from a prophet is much. By Allah, it will never leave me as long as I live. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Salih al-Murri, from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Sari; and Abd al-Aziz al-Basri is well known, there is no harm in him; Anas alone narrated it."
"6695","6693 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qat'i'i narrated to us, they said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, says: O son of Adam, one is for you, and one is for Me, and one is between Me and you: As for that which is for Me, then worship Me and do not associate anything with Me. And as for that which is for you, then whatever you did - or of deed - I will repay you for it in full. And as for that which is between Me and you, then from you is supplication and upon Me is answering. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Salih al-Murri; Anas alone narrated it."
"6696","Sa'id ibn Zarbi from al-Hasan from him. 6694 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Zarbi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of the women of the warriors. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn Zarbi; and Sa'id is not strong."
"6697","Abu Rabi'ah al-Iyadi from al-Hasan from him. 6695 - Nasr ibn Abbad narrated to us; Abu Ahmad narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Rabi'ah, from al-Hasan, from Anas, raised: He said: Paradise longs for three: Ali and Ammar - and I think he said - and Abu Dharr. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Abu Rabi'ah; and he is a Kufan; al-Hasan ibn Salih and Sharik narrated from him. And as for this hadith, none narrated it from him except al-Hasan ibn Salih."
"6698","Tammam ibn Najih from al-Hasan. 6696 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Mubashshir ibn Isma'il al-Halabi narrated to us; Tammam ibn Najih narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two guardian angels who raise to Allah what they guarded in a day, and the blessed and exalted reads at the beginning of the scroll and at its end seeking forgiveness, except that the blessed and exalted says: I have forgiven My servant what is between the two ends of this scroll. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Tammam ibn Najih; and Tammam is sound in hadith; and none narrated this hadith other than him, and he was not followed in it; Anas alone narrated it."
"6699","Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah from al-Hasan from him. 6697 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the worst of rulers is the crushing one. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it with this wording except Abd al-Karim; and it has been narrated from other than Anas; Abu Barzah and Abid ibn Amr and others narrated it; and this Abd al-Karim is a Basran."
"6700","Isma'il ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from him. 6698 - Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of my Companions is like salt in food; food is not good except with it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Isma'il ibn Muslim; and none narrated it from him except Abu Mu'awiyah; and Isma'il ibn Muslim, al-A'mash and al-Thawri and a large group narrated from him, though he is not a memorizer; and the group tolerated his hadith; Anas alone narrated it."
"6701","6699 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two tongues in this world will have two tongues in the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Isma'il ibn Muslim; Anas alone narrated it."
"6702","6700 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman Abu Bahr ibn Uthman al-Bakrawi narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar."
"6703","6701 - And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade the sale of muhaffalat and said: Whoever buys them has the option, meaning when he milks them."
"6704","6702 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the lavatory, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Isma'il ibn Muslim."
"6705","6703 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us; Quraysh ibn Anas narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim and another man - Abu Bakr said, meaning Amr ibn Ubayd - from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he made qunut until he died. Abu Bakr said: Thus narrated Isma'il ibn Muslim and Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas. And Muhammad ibn Sirin and Abu Mijlaz and Qatadah narrated this hadith, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut for a month. And those who narrated it, that he made qunut for a month, are reliable. And Isma'il ibn Muslim, we have explained his weakness. And Amr ibn Ubayd, we dispense with mentioning him, due to his fame for evil opinion."
"6706","6704 - Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has the Hereafter as his intention, Allah, blessed and exalted, makes richness in his heart, and gathers his affairs for him, and removes poverty from before his eyes, and the world comes to him humbled; so he does not wake in the morning except rich, nor reach the evening except rich. And whoever has the world as his intention and his quest, Allah makes poverty before his eyes, so he does not wake in the morning except poor, nor reach the evening except poor. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except Isma'il ibn Muslim; Anas alone narrated it."
"6707","6705 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was saying the talbiyah: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; Labbayk, there is no partner for You, Labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"6708","Ishaq ibn al-Rabi' from al-Hasan from him. 6706 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Umar ibn Sahl narrated to us; Ishaq ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: I do not recognize today anything of what we were upon at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except this prayer, though you have innovated in it what you have innovated. And we do not know of Ishaq ibn al-Rabi' narrating from al-Hasan, from Anas, except this hadith; and he is a Basran man, there is no harm in him."
"6709","al-Fadl ibn Dalham from al-Hasan from him. 6707 - Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Dalham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed a man who leads a people while they dislike him, and a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and a man who hears: Come to success, and does not answer. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Hasan, from Anas, except al-Fadl ibn Dalham; and he is not a memorizer; and he is a famous Basran; Anas alone narrated it. Humayd ibn al-Hakam from al-Hasan from him."
"6710","6708 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us; Amr ibn Asim al-Burjumi narrated to us; Humayd ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two blessings in which many people are cheated: health and free time. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this angle with this chain. And Humayd ibn al-Hakam is a Basran; he narrated from al-Hasan, from Anas, another hadith. And Amr ibn Asim al-Burjumi is well known; Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad and others narrated from him. Abu Raja Muhammad ibn Sayf - a Basran - from al-Hasan from him."
"6711","6709 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us; Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from al-Hasan, he said: Anas was asked about the nushrah. He said: It was mentioned to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it. He said: It is from the work of Satan. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Miskin ibn Bukayr. And Miskin is a Harranian, trustworthy, well known. And Shu'bah did not musnad from Abu Raja except this hadith. And this Abu Raja is well known, a Basran; his name is Muhammad ibn Sayf; Shu'bah narrated from him, and Yazid ibn Zuray' and Isma'il ibn Ulayyah and Nuh ibn Qays al-Tahi and Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated from him."
"6712","Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Anas. 6710 - Abu Kamil narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad - meaning Ibn Sirin - he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about the qunut. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut after the bowing."
"6713","6711 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"6714","6712 - And with his chain, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar and said: The donkeys have been eaten. And one who came said: The donkeys have been exhausted, O Messenger of Allah. So he ordered a caller who called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you domestic donkeys, for they are filth. He said: So the pots were overturned with the meat. Up to here is the hadith of Abd al-Wahhab."
"6715","6713 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us; Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad - meaning Ibn Sirin - from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it; and he added in it: And people plundered sheep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, who called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you plunder. And this place which Asim narrated from Ayyub, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Asim ibn Hilal."
"6716","6714 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attacked Khaybar early in the morning, while they had come out with spades. So he said: Allah is greatest; Khaybar is ruined. Indeed when we descend into the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who are warned. And this hadith, Ibn Uyaynah and Ma'mar narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas."
"6717","6715 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of Eid, then delivered the sermon, then slaughtered, and said: Whoever slaughtered before our prayer, let him repeat."
"6718","6716 - Ahmad ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Mazini narrated to us; Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that - or - his gray hair did not reach that. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Wuhayb, from Ayyub."
"6719","6717 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us; Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas."
"6720","6718 - And al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the Jamrat al-Aqabah, then left, sacrificed, and called the barber. So he shaved one side of his head and gave it to Abu Talhah, and shaved the other side, and the people divided it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn and Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"6721","6719 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Anas; that when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Or as he said. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas. But thus said Abd al-Rahman, from Hammad. And two memorizers narrated it from Abd al-Rahman: one of them Amr ibn Ali, and the other Sulayman Sahib al-Basri."
"6722","6720 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abd al-Mu'min ibn Abbad informed us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: They used to write the beginnings of their wills: This is what so-and-so son of so-and-so bequeathed; he bequeathed that we bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that Paradise is true, and that the Fire is true, and that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt in it, and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves; and he bequeathed to those he left behind with what Ibrahim bequeathed his sons: O my sons, Allah has chosen the religion for you, so die not except as Muslims. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Abd al-Mu'min ibn Abbad; and he is a man from the people of Basra, there is no harm in him. And Hisham narrated it from Muhammad, from Anas. And it is strange from the hadith of Ayyub; Nasr alone narrated it from Abd al-Mu'min."
"6723","Ibn Awn from Muhammad from Anas. 6721 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden that a townsman sell for a bedouin. And this hadith, Ibn Awn and Yunus and Hisham and Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated it from Muhammad."
"6724","6722 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: When Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah was born, Abu Talhah said to me: Take him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to tahnik him. So I brought him to him while he was in a pen marking sheep. So he tahnik him with a date, and the boy began smacking it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beloved of the Ansar is dates. And this hadith, Hatim ibn Wardan and Ibn Abi Adi narrated it from Ibn Awn."
"6725","6723 - al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dharra' narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Nu'man - trustworthy - narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be so gentle with us that he would say to a small brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do? And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, except with this chain; and it is strange from Ibn Awn."
"6726","6724 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to us, they said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Abbad - meaning Ibn al-Awwam - narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the jamrah on the day of sacrifice, then left, sacrificed, then shaved. So he shaved one side of his head - I think he said: the right side of his head - and gave it to Abu Talhah, and shaved his left side and divided it among the people. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas, except from the hadith of Abbad, from Ibn Awn; and it is strange from Ibn Awn."
"6727","6725 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Anas; that when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Or as he said."
"6728","Hisham ibn Hassan from Muhammad from Anas. 6726 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of sacrifice, then left, sacrificed his camels while the barber was sitting. So he inclined his head to him. He said: Shave. So he shaved a side of his head and divided it - meaning among the people - and said to him: Shave the left side. So he shaved it, and handed it to me, and I handed it to Abu Talhah."
"6729","6727 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: And a man asked him about a man who accuses his wife. So he said: I asked Anas about that while I thought he had knowledge about it. So he said: The first to do li'an was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Hilal ibn Umayyah accused his wife with Sharik ibn al-Sahma, and he was the first to do li'an. And Sharik was the brother of al-Bara ibn Malik through his mother. So he did li'an between them both, and said: Watch him: if she brings him white, straight-haired, then he is for Hilal ibn Umayyah; and if she brings him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin-legged, then he is for Sharik. He said: Then I was informed that she brought him dark-eyed, curly-haired, thin-legged. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Anas, except Hisham."
"6730","6728 - Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar. Then a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been eaten. And another came and said: The donkeys have been exhausted. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, who called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for they are filth. So the pots were overturned."
"6731","6729 - And with his chain: And people plundered sheep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, who called out: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you plunder."
"6732","6730 - And with his chain, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that; but Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam."
"6733","6731 - Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ubulli narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Hasan ibn Ja'far narrated to us; my father and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother loves this surah, meaning: Say: He is Allah, One. So he said: Give your brother glad tidings of Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Ja'far ibn Hasan; and he is sound in hadith."
"6734","6732 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari and Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, they said: al-Salt ibn Muhammad al-Kharaki narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, and from Sinan Abu Rabi'ah, and from al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, from Anas; that his mother took a mudd of barley, crushed it and ground it, and took a skin containing ghee and squeezed it. Then she sent me with it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to him while he was among his companions, and I invited him. So he said: And those with me? So I came, meaning to Abu Talhah, and said: He said to me: And those with me? He said: So Abu Talhah went out and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is only something Umm Sulaym made. He said: Then bring it to me. So he placed his hand upon it, or the place of his hand in it, and said: Admit ten upon me. So they ate until they were full. Then he said: Admit ten upon me. So they ate, until he counted forty. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate and stood up. So I kept looking, and nothing of it had decreased. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"6735","6733 - And Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah mentioned; Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be so gentle with us that he would say to a small brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do? And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Muhammad ibn Marwan."
"6736","6734 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Ta'i narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: When Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, he began looking at it and twisting it with a stick, or turning it with a stick, and said: Indeed he was handsome. Anas said: So I said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing him, or pressing kisses on him."
"6737","6735 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us; Za'idah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: They used to write the beginnings of their wills: This is what so-and-so son of so-and-so bequeathed ... And he mentioned the hadith. And we have mentioned it from Ayyub, from Muhammad."
"6738","6736 - Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, as far as I know, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden that a townsman sell for a bedouin."
"6739","6737 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: Abu Quhafah was brought on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and his head and beard were as if white thaghamah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they change it and avoid black for him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Muhammad ibn Salamah; and it is strange from Muhammad, from Anas; and he was not in Basra."
"6740","Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal from Muhammad. 6738 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Asim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that; but Abu Bakr dyed with henna."
"6741","6739 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Jabalah narrated to us; Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: Anas said: Umm Sulaym had a cup from which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink. Then it broke and was mended with a band. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink from it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, except Abu Hamzah."
"6742","6740 - Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Mikhwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Isra'il narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that he had with him a small staff of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then he died and it was buried with him, between his side and his shirt. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Isra'il, from Asim, from Muhammad, from Anas, except Mikhwal ibn Ibrahim. And Mikhwal is truthful, and there was Shi'ism in him, and it was tolerated despite that."
"6743","Khalid al-Hadhdha from Muhammad. 6741 - Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us; Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Anas: Did Umar make qunut? He said: One better than Umar made qunut: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut. And we do not know of Khalid musnad from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6744","Yunus ibn Ubayd from Muhammad from Anas. 6742 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: One who prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the dawn prayer narrated to me: that when he raised his head from the second rak'ah, he stood a while. Abu Bakr said: And some people mentioned that he is Anas; and it resembles, because it has been narrated from Muhammad, from Anas, that he made qunut after the bowing."
"6745","6743 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Yunus, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden that a townsman sell for a bedouin."
"6746","6744 - Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us; Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, except Khalid; and it is only known from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas."
"6747","al-Rabi' ibn Subayh from. 6745 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us; al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas and Ubadah ibn al-Samit, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like; and silver for silver, like for like. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Anas, except al-Rabi' ibn Subayh; and it is only known from other than the hadith of al-Rabi', from Muhammad, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Ubadah."
"6748","Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Muhammad. 6746 - Ahmad ibn Ubadah narrated to us; Hafs ibn Sulayman informed us; Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim. And this hadith, only Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated it from Kathir. And Hafs is very weak in hadith. And all that is narrated from Anas about: Seeking knowledge is an obligation, its chains are all weak. And we mentioned this hadith only to explain the defect in it, and that Muhammad narrated it from Anas."
"6749","Salamah ibn Alqamah from Muhammad. 6747 - al-Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden that a townsman sell for a bedouin. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Salamah ibn Alqamah, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal."
"6750","Muhammad ibn Amr al-Waqifi - a clan of Banu Waqif of the Ansar - from Muhammad. 6748 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father informed me; Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: He did not reach that; but Abu Bakr dyed with henna. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas. And we do not know of Muhammad ibn Amr narrating from Ibn Sirin, from Anas, except this hadith. And he narrated from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, other than a hadith."
"6751","Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik from Muhammad. 6749 - Abu al-Rabi' al-Jahdari al-A'raj, I think him Khalid ibn Muhammad, narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Ash'ath - meaning Ibn Abd al-Malik - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas; that Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hungry; is there anything with you? She said: A mudd, or half a mudd of barley. He said: We will invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for it. So she made it a loaf. Anas said: So Abu Talhah sent me and said: Go and invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah invites you ... And he mentioned the hadith. And we do not know of Ash'ath narrating from Muhammad, from Anas, except this hadith; and none narrated it from Ash'ath except Abu Asim."
"6752","Ash'ath ibn Sawwar from Muhammad. 6750 - Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Ubulli narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: When it was the day of Khaybar, the people fell upon donkeys. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller, who called out: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys. And we do not know of Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrating from Muhammad, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6753","Jarir ibn Hazim from Muhammad. 6751 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sahib al-Sabiri and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad ibn Qumayr narrated to us, they said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: There was a fright in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse of Abu Talhah that was slow, or in which was slowness. Then when he returned, he said: Indeed we found him a sea. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Muhammad, from Anas, except from the narration of Jarir from him; and none narrated it from Jarir except al-Husayn ibn Muhammad."
"6754","6752 - And with his chain, he said: When Ibn Ziyad was brought the head of al-Husayn, he began looking at it and turning it with a stick. So he said: Indeed he was handsome, or a word like it. So Anas said: So I said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or long did I see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - kissing him, or pressing kisses on him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Jarir except Husayn ibn Muhammad; this speech is its wording, or its meaning."
"6755","Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani from Anas. Khalid al-Hadhdha from Bakr. 6753 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah."
"6756","6754 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Bakr, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"6757","Habib from Bakr. 6755 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us; Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for both together, meaning Hajj and Umrah. So I met Ibn Umar and informed him. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram for Hajj. So I returned to Anas and informed him of the saying of Ibn Umar. So he said: They only count us as children, or we were only children. And we do not know of Habib narrating from Bakr, from Ibn Umar, except this hadith; and none narrated it from Habib except Sa'id ibn Amir."
"6758","Yunus from Bakr. 6756 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us; Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Bakr, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah. And we do not know of Yusuf narrating from Bakr, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6759","Humayd from Bakr. 6757 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr, from Anas, who said: And I asked him: With what did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter ihram? He said: He entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah."
"6760","6758 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, from Anas. Mubarak ibn Fadalah from Bakr."
"6761","6759 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Talhah met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hungry. So he returned to his family and said to Umm Sulaym: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hungry; is there anything with you? She said: A mudd, or half a mudd of barley flour. He said: Then we will invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for it. So she made from it a loaf. Anas said: So Abu Talhah sent me and said: Go and invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah invites you. So he said to his companions: Stand up to Abu Talhah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and with him some eighty-odd of his companions. So I said: Did you not tell him what is with us? I said: I invited him, and he said to them: Stand up. So Abu Talhah said: It is only a small thing. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said to him. He said to him: By Allah, it is only a loaf; I saw you hungry, so I made it for you. So he said: Bring it to me. He said: So I brought it to him, and he placed the loaf in the bowl. Then he said: Is there anything with you? I said: No, except that there may be a little something in the skin. He said: Bring it to me. So I brought it to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began squeezing until something came out upon the mouth of the skin. So he took it with his index finger. Then he said: In the name of Allah. Then he wiped the loaf with it, and it swelled. Then he squeezed again, and it came out, and he took it with his finger. Then he wiped the loaf with it, and it swelled. Then he squeezed a third time, and something came out of it. So he took it with his finger. Then he said: In the name of Allah, and wiped the loaf with it. So it swelled until the bowl was filled. So he said: Give permission to ten. So I admitted ten. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand and spread his fingers in the middle of the bowl - or he said: and spread his fingers in the middle of the loaf - and said: Eat in the name of Allah. So they ate until they were full. Then he said: Call ten others for me. And the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hidden in the middle of the loaf. And he said: Eat in the name of Allah. So they ate until they were full. Then they went out. So they kept entering ten by ten, eating until they were full; and they were some eighty-odd men. And the middle of the loaf remained. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Bakr, from Anas, except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"6762","Sa'id ibn Ubayd from Bakr. 6760 - Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us; Abu Qutaybah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, blessed and exalted: O son of Adam, as long as you supplicate Me and hope in Me, I will forgive you for what is in you, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this angle. And none narrated it from Bakr, from Anas, except Sa'id ibn Ubayd. And Sa'id ibn Ubayd, they said: Sa'id ibn Ubayd; and they said: Sa'id ibn Ubaydillah; and there is no harm in him."
"6763","6761 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sahib al-Sabiri narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I used to pour for my uncles a mixture of unripe and ripe dates. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: That wine has been made unlawful. He said: So we poured it out, while it was their drink that day. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Bakr except from this angle."
"6764","6762 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Anas; that a woman entered upon A'ishah, and with her were two daughters of hers. He said: So A'ishah gave her three dates. So she gave each one of them a date. Then she took a date to place it in her mouth. He said: So the two girls looked at her. He said: So she split it in two halves, and gave each one of them half, and went out. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and A'ishah told him of what the woman did, or of the deed of the woman. So he said: She has entered Paradise by that. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except with this chain. And Ubaydullah ibn Fadalah is a Basran. And they are brothers: al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, and Ubaydullah ibn Fadalah, and al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah. And all of them narrated; and there is no harm in them."
"6765","Abu Qilabah from Anas. Ayyub from Abu Qilabah. 6763 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah four, and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah two."
"6766","6764 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah - and I know it only from Anas - he said: A group from Ukl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek milk camels for us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come out to the camels. So they went out to the camels, and obtained of their milk and urine until they became fat. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and drove off the camels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who went in their pursuit. The sun had not yet declined when they were brought. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding them: their hands and feet were cut off, their eyes were branded, and they were thrown in the Harrah, asking for water but not given water, until they died. Abu Qilabah said: They killed, stole, disbelieved, and waged war against Allah, blessed and exalted, and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6767","6765 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to two horned rams and slaughtered them with his hand. And this hadith, we preserve it only from the hadith of Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub."
"6768","6766 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a camel-driver driving, called Anjashah: O Anjashah, gently drive the glass vessels."
"6769","6767 - And al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us; Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter upon Umm Sulaym, and she would spread for him a leather mat, and he would nap upon it. And he sweated much, so she would take his sweat and place it in her perfume. And she would spread for him the khumrah, and he would pray upon it. Thus said Wuhayb, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas. And Abd al-Wahhab said: from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas."
"6770","6768 - And Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the supper is placed and the prayer is established, then begin with the supper. Thus narrated Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman. And we do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, except Muhammad."
"6771","6769 / 1 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub and Khalid. 6769 / 2 - And Salamah narrated it to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was ordered to double the adhan and make the iqamah odd."
"6772","6770 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; Simak ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was ordered to double the adhan and make the iqamah odd, except the iqamah, meaning he says: The prayer has been established, twice."
"6773","6771 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us; Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you pray and do not know whether you finished upon even or upon odd, then prostrate twice. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this angle. And none narrated it from Ayyub except Abbad ibn Mansur; and none from Abbad except Rayhan ibn Sa'id. And Rayhan ibn Sa'id is a Basran; the people of hadith wrote from him: Ali ibn al-Madini and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah and Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and others. And he narrated many hadiths from Abbad, from Ayyub, which none narrated from him other than him; and they were tolerated from him despite his singling them out, without denial against him."
"6774","6772 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us; Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love. He said: And he looked at a boy. Anas said: He was of my age. So he said: If this lives - I think he said: old age will not return until the Hour is established. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, except Abbad."
"6775","6773 - And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us; Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of my nation will meet Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Abbad."
"6776","6774 - And with his chain, he said: Abu Talhah cauterized me while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive, and more than one of the Ansar attended that."
"6777","6775 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted a household of the Ansar ruqyah for the scorpion sting and the ant bite. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it also except Abbad."
"6778","6776 - And with his chain, and more: and Salamah ibn Shabib narrated it to us; Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us; Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas - the two come close in their hadith, and the wording is the wording of Ma'mar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted, supports this religion with men who have no share. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Ma'mar and Abbad ibn Mansur. And we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ma'mar except Rabah. And Rabah is a Yemeni, trustworthy. And Ibrahim ibn Khalid is trustworthy."
"6779","6777 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged regarding the dead-end road which is approached from every place: when its people dispute about it, its width is seven cubits. And he judged that whatever you have enclosed is yours, and whatever they have not enclosed is for Allah and His Messenger. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except with this chain. And none narrated it from Abd al-Rahim except Ali ibn Sa'id; and he heard it only from him, and he was not followed in it; and he was trustworthy."
"6780","6778 - Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not be established until people boast of mosques. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Salamah, with this chain."
"6781","6779 - Yahya ibn Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us; Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us; Rushdayn ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, except Jarir ibn Hazim; and none from Jarir except Rushdayn. And Jarir ibn Hazim also narrated, from Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. So we held back from the hadith of Thabit, because Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit, from Anas. And Khalid and Asim narrated this hadith from Abu Qilabah, from Anas."
"6782","6780 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that a Jew crushed the head of a girl between two stones until she died. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that it be done to him likewise. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, except Ma'mar."
"6783","6781 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed seven for the virgin and three for the previously married. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The sunnah of the virgin is seven, and the previously married three. And Ibn Ishaq musnad it."
"6784","6782 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Raqashi narrated it to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The sunnah regarding the virgin is seven, and regarding the previously married three. Abu Bakr said, meaning he stays with the virgin seven and with the previously married three."
"6785","6783 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us; Amr ibn Sufyan al-Qut'i narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to his companions: You are better than your children, and your children are better than their children. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain. And al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far was a worshipful man and was not a memorizer; and his hadith was tolerated despite his little memorization, due to the goodness of his worship."
"6786","6784 - Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes, let him leave until he knows what he says."
"6787","6785 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would travel and prolong absence, then pray two rak'ahs until he returns."
"6788","Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu Qilabah. 6786 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr; and the firmest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar; and the most truthful of them in modesty is Uthman; and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal. And every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. And this hadith, more than one narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The most merciful of my nation. And he mentioned the hadith until it became: And every nation has a trustworthy one. Then he mentioned this place from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the rest of the speech from Abu Qilabah, mursal. And Abd al-Wahhab made all the speech from Anas entirely. And al-Thawri followed Abd al-Wahhab in this narration: Qabisah narrated it from al-Thawri, from Khalid and Asim."
"6789","6787 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated it to us; Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid and Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr; and the firmest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar; and the most modest is Uthman; and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal; and the best reciter of them is Zayd ibn Thabit. And every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, except Sufyan."
"6790","6788 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, who said: Bilal was ordered to double the adhan and make the iqamah odd."
"6791","6789 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam informed us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar would not recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. And this hadith, thus narrated Yahya ibn Adam from al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas. And other than Yahya ibn Adam narrated it from al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Abu Na'amah, from Anas."
"6792","6790 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it with it to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faryabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid, from Abu Na'amah, from Anas, with the like of it."
"6793","Humayd ibn Hilal from Anas. 6791 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas."
"6794","6792 - And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated it to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas, who said: I was indeed riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was saying the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Humayd ibn Hilal except Ayyub. And this hadith indicates in it that Abu Talhah was saying the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and did not deny it; because Anas did not say in this hadith: So I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying the talbiyah; he only said: I heard him, meaning Abu Talhah."
"6795","6793 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas."
"6796","6794 - And Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated it to us; Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of Ja'far when he was struck, while his eyes were shedding tears."
"6797","6795 - And Ibn Ma'in and Ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: As if I am looking at the dust of the procession of Jibril (peace be upon him), rising in Banu Ghanm, while he intends Banu Qurayzah. Abu Bakr said: Jarir ibn Hazim is trustworthy; and he became confused, so his son confined him in his confusion and did not let him narrate. So his hadith came out sound."
"6798","Anas ibn Sirin from Anas. Ayyub from Anas ibn Sirin. 6796 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter upon Umm Sulaym, and she would spread for him a leather mat, and he would nap upon it. So she would take his sweat and place it in her perfume. And she would spread for him the khumrah, and he would pray upon it. Thus narrated Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas. And Wuhayb ibn Khalid opposed him: he narrated it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas. And the hadith is well known from the hadith of Anas ibn Sirin: Ayyub and Ibn Awn and Shu'bah narrated it from Anas ibn Sirin. And we do not know of Ayyub narrating from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6799","Habib ibn al-Shahid from Anas ibn Sirin. 6797 - al-Abbas ibn Yazid al-Bahrani narrated to us; Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to us; Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica the fatty tail of an Arab ram, neither small nor large: it is melted, then a portion is drunk from it each day. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Habib ibn al-Shahid except Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq. And Abd al-Khaliq is a famous Basran; Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi and Uthman ibn Talut and Hafs ibn Mahbub and others narrated from him. And Habib did not narrate from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6800","Hisham ibn Hassan from Anas ibn Sirin. 6798 - Muslim ibn Junadah ibn Muslim narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he prescribed for sciatica the fatty tail of an Arab ram, neither small nor large: it is melted, divided into three portions, and a portion is drunk from it each day. Anas ibn Sirin said: So I prescribed that to a large group, and they recovered by the permission of Allah."
"6801","Shu'bah from Anas ibn Sirin. 6799 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man of the Ansar made food and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came to him, and a mat was spread for him, and he prayed two rak'ahs upon it. So a man of the family of al-Jarud said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? He said: I never saw him pray it before that day."
"6802","6800 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was come to by a man of the Ansar, who said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you came to us and prayed - meaning in our house - and we took it as a prayer place. So he came to him and prayed in his house the Duha prayer, two rak'ahs. And we do not know of Shu'bah narrating from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas, except these two hadiths."
"6803","Bakkar ibn Mahan from Anas ibn Sirin. 6801 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Bakkar ibn Mahan narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Sirin narrating from Anas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon his mount."
"6804","Hammad ibn Salamah from Anas ibn Sirin. 6802 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made qunut in the dawn prayer - I think he said: after the bowing. And this hadith, we preserved it only from Ibn Marzuq, from Mu'ammal, thus. And it has been narrated from Anas from angles."
"6805","Yahya ibn Sirin from Anas. 6803 - I heard some of our companions narrating from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from his brother Yahya ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: The talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk, a true Hajj, worship and servitude."
"6806","6804 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from his brother Yahya ibn Sirin, he said: The talbiyah of Anas was: Labbayk, a true Hajj, worship and servitude. And perhaps he said: He used to say that when he finished his talbiyah. And Hammad did not musnad it, and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl musnad it. And Yahya ibn Sirin did not narrate from Anas except with this hadith."
"6807","From the hadith of Thabit from Anas. 6805 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Thabit and Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Imran said: Four will come out of the Fire; and Thabit said: Two. Then Allah, blessed and exalted, will order that they be returned, or they will be returned to the Fire. Then the last of them will turn and say: O my Lord, I thought when You took me out of it that You would not return me to it. So Allah, blessed and exalted, will order him to Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit and Abu Imran, from Anas."
"6808","6806 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh informed us; Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that a man stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Where is my father? He said: In the Fire. Then when he turned away, he called him and said: My father and your father are in the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Thabit, from Anas, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6809","6807 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): some said: I will not marry women; and some said: I will not eat meat; and some said: I will not sleep on a bed; and some said: I fast and do not break. So that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is the matter with people who say such and such? But I pray and sleep, and fast and break, and marry women. So whoever turns away from my sunnah is not from me. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Thabit, from Anas, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6810","6808 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard in it a movement. So I said: What is this? They said: The daughter of Bilal. And I entered Paradise and heard in it a movement. So I said: What is this? They said: This is al-Ghumaysa daughter of Milhan, and she is Umm Sulaym."
"6811","6809 - Muhammad narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come out of the Fire, and Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: How did you find your abode? So he will say: O my Lord, the worst abode. So Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: Would you ransom yourself from it with the world in gold? So he will say: Yes. So the blessed and exalted will say to him: You lied; I asked you for what is less than that, and you did not do it. And a man of the people of Paradise will be brought, and it will be said to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? So he will say: The best abode. So he will say: So what do you ask Me? So he will say: I ask You only to return me to the world and be killed in Your path ten times. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Thabit, from Anas, except Hammad."
"6812","6810 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah from one of his expeditions or journeys, and the blacks of Madinah were dancing before him: Muhammad has come, a righteous man, with their speech that. And Anas did not mention that he forbade them, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6813","6811 - And with his chain; that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him sheep between two mountains. So he came to his people and said: O my people, accept Islam, for Muhammad gives a giving that does not fear poverty."
"6814","6812 - And with his chain; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given al-Kawthar. So I struck with my hand upon its watering place, and it was a strong-smelling musk. And its pebbles were pearls. And its two banks - I think he said - domes flowing upon the earth, flowing, not cracked."
"6815","6813 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was when he went out to Madinah. And Abu Bakr - may Allah have mercy on him - was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - had come to Sham, so he was known. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not known. So they would say to Abu Bakr: Who is this who is before you? So he would say: This is the one who guides the path. Then when they drew near Madinah, he sent to the Ansar, and they came. Anas said: I never saw a day more beautiful nor brighter than the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us; nor a day uglier nor darker than the day in which he died, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6816","6814 - With his chain; he said: No person was more beloved to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they would not stand up for him because of what they knew of his dislike (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for that."
"6817","6815 - With his chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lick his fingers when he ate."
"6818","6816 - With his chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three qualities, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be more beloved to him than anything else, that he love a person only for Allah, and that being cast into the Fire be more beloved to him than returning to Judaism or Christianity."
"6819","6817 - With his chain; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him, and whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is recorded against him; but if he does it, one evil deed is recorded."
"6820","6818 - With his chain; that Abu Talhah used to shoot in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was an archer, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was behind him. When he shot, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his figure to see where his arrow landed, so he would push the chest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him and say: Like this, no arrow will hit you."
"6821","6819 - With his chain; he said: I saw the people hastening to the pillars when the caller to prayer gave the call for Maghrib prayer, praying the two units before Maghrib."
"6822","6820 - Abu Bakr said: Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us this hadith: Muhammad ibn as-Salt Abu Yala ath-Thawri narrated to us, Abu Safwan al-Makki narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Thabit, from Anas, with something similar. This hadith has been reported from Thabit from Anas by more than one, and we do not know of Ata ibn Abi Rabah reporting from Thabit from Anas except this hadith."
"6823","6821 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas; that a group of eighty men from the people of Makkah came down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Mount at-Tanim at Fajr prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized them peacefully and pardoned them, so Allah revealed: And He is the One Who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them, to the end of the verse."
"6824","6822 - Ali ibn Sahl narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When Allah created Adam and fashioned him, Iblis began circling around him; when he saw him as a hollow creation, he knew that he would not refrain from disobeying, or a phrase like it; and I think he raised it as a Prophetic report."
"6825","6823 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships and Hell is surrounded by desires."
"6826","6824 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to descend from the pulpit on Friday, and a man would speak to him about a need, until his place of prayer."
"6827","6825 - Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet: that he recited upon the pulpit: When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain He made it crumble; he said: Like this, and he spread his palm and placed the thumb upon the little finger. Humayd said to him: Do you narrate something like this? So he struck his chest and said: Who are you, Humayd? Anas narrates it from the Messenger of Allah, and you say this to me? This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it except Hammad from Thabit."
"6828","6826 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Abu Ubaydah and Abu Talhah. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Hammad."
"6829","6827 - Al-Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn al-Hakam al-Basri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleeping in the house of Umm Sulaym, and she came to him while he was saying words of remembrance of returning to Allah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you say that? He said: Because of an army coming from Iraq seeking a man from Madinah whom Allah will protect from them; when they ascend the desert plain at Dhul-Hulayfah they will be swallowed by the earth, so their first will not reach their last nor their last their first until the Day of Resurrection, and their places of death will be scattered. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will they all be swallowed while their places of death are scattered? He said: Among them, or in them, are those who were compelled. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Hammad, and none reported it from Hammad except this man we mentioned."
"6830","6828 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala as-Sanani narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, when the verse Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet was revealed, sat in his house and said: I am among the people of Hell; I used to raise my voice over the Messenger of Allah. He was missed, so he said: Why do I not see Thabit? Is he ill? Sad said: He is my neighbor, and I know of no illness in him. So Sad mentioned that to Thabit, and said: The Messenger of Allah has missed you. He said: This verse was revealed, and I used to raise my voice over the Messenger of Allah, so I am among the people of Hell. So Sad mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, and he said: Rather he is among the people of Paradise. This hadith was reported by Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit, and the noblest who reported it from Thabit is Sulayman at-Taymi, and we do not know of Sulayman at-Taymi reporting as a connected chain from Thabit except this hadith."
"6831","6829 - Al-Walid ibn Sufyan al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sayyar, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by children and greeted them. We do not know of Sayyar reporting as a connected chain from Thabit from Anas except this hadith, and it has been reported from Thabit by a group."
"6832","6830 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he practiced continuous fasting, so some people continued fasting, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a way that would make the extremists abandon their extremism. I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"6833","6831 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet, with something similar."
"6834","6832 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, even if it is a sacrificial camel."
"6835","6833 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned white-and-black rams."
"6836","6834 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet visited a man who had become like a fledgling chick, and said: What did you used to supplicate? Or: What did you ask your Lord for well-being? He said: I used to say: O Allah, whatever You would punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. He said: Glory be to Allah, you will never bear it, or you cannot bear it; why did you not say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire? So the man said it and recovered. This hadith has been reported from Humayd from Thabit by a group, and reported from Thabit by more than one, so we sufficed with those we named."
"6837","6835 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet saw a man being supported between two men, and the Prophet said: What is wrong with him? They said: He vowed to perform Hajj walking. He said: Command him to ride, for Allah is free of need of his tormenting himself. This hadith has been reported by more than one from Humayd from Thabit, so we sufficed with those we named."
"6838","6836 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Fayyad and Ismail ibn Bashir ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The prayer would be established, then a man would intercept the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak to him about a need until some of the people would doze. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Humayd from Thabit from Anas except Abd al-Ala."
"6839","6837/1 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Amr ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas."
"6840","6837/2 - And I found in my book, from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar: Said ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas."
"6841","6838 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, meaning Ibn Sawwar, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment."
"6842","6839 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet passed by a graveyard and heard a sound from a grave, and said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have made you hear the sound of this grave, or the sound of the one in the grave. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Humayd from Thabit from Anas except al-Mutamir."
"6843","6840 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The vision of the believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Shubah."
"6844","6841 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, would stand until one would say: He has forgotten; and when he raised his head from prostration, he would sit until we would say: He has forgotten."
"6845","6842 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet: that when he raised his head from bowing he would stand until we would say: He has forgotten, due to the length of standing. This hadith was reported by Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit from Anas."
"6846","6843 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet."
"6847","6844 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet who said: Patience is at the first shock. And Uthman ibn Umar said: Patience is at the first shock."
"6848","6845 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any of his supplications except in the prayer for rain."
"6849","6846 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Shubah, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with the one he loves. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Shubah from Anas except Baqiyyah."
"6850","6847 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah used to supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. And Hammad ibn Salamah reported it."
"6851","6848 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every treacherous person there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection."
"6852","6849 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling with a camel-driver chanting for the women, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, your driving with the glass vessels. And Hammad ibn Salamah reported it."
"6853","6850 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd as-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah said: None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him; and if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep us alive if life is better for us, and cause us to die if death is better for us."
"6854","6851 - Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated it to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, from the Prophet, with something similar."
"6855","6852 - Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from Shubah, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat. This hadith: Abu Amir was not followed in his narration from Shubah; rather it is reported from Shubah from Anas ibn Sirin from Anas from the Prophet, and Hammad ibn Salamah reported it from Thabit from Anas."
"6856","6853 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas; that Abu Talhah would hardly fast voluntarily during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of military expeditions; then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, they never saw him eating except on the day of Adha or Fitr."
"6857","6854 - Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shubah, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet and Abu Bakr and Umar used to begin recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. We do not know of al-Amash reporting from Shubah except this hadith, and we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-Amash except Ammar ibn Ruzayq."
"6858","6855 - Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas."
"6859","6856 - Muhammad ibn Rizqullah al-Kalwadhani narrated it to us, Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Ansar gathered and said: Let us go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him to make our water flowing, for the water-drawing camels have become hard upon us. So they gathered at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Welcome to the Ansar, welcome to the Ansar, welcome to the Ansar, three times; you will not ask me for anything today except that I give it to you, and I will not ask anything for you today except that I am given. So some of them said to one another: Seize his supplication and ask for forgiveness. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we came for you to supplicate to Allah for forgiveness for us. So he said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar and the children of the children of the Ansar. We do not know of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad reporting as a connected chain from Thabit from Anas except this hadith, and we do not know of anyone reporting it from Yazid except Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim."
"6860","6857 - Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib at-Tai narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: There was a black man in the mosque who died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about him. They said: He died. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to his grave and prayed over him. This hadith was reported by Shubah from Habib ibn ash-Shahid from Thabit from Anas, that the Prophet prayed over a grave. We do not know of anyone reporting this hadith from Habib except Shubah; we mentioned it from Abu Amir, though he is below Habib, because Abu Amir has more complete wording for it."
"6861","6858 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, distress began to overwhelm him, so Fatimah supported him against her chest and said: O my distress, for the distress of my father! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no distress upon your father after today. And she said: O my father, how near he is to his Lord! O my father, the Gardens of Firdaws are his abode! O my father, to Gabriel we announce his death! O my father, he answered a Lord Who called him! Anas said: Fatimah said, or he said, then she said: O Anas, did your selves feel at ease to throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! This hadith has been reported by more than one, and some of them said: from Thabit, without saying: from Anas, except at the end of the speech, meaning the speech of Fatimah."
"6862","6859 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most generous of people and the bravest of people. The people of Madinah were frightened one night, so he set out toward the sound and met them coming back, upon a horse belonging to Abu Talhah, unsaddled, with a sword around his neck, saying: O people, you have no cause for fear, you have no cause for fear. And he said to the horse: We found it to be a sea, or: It is indeed a sea. The horse had belonged to Abu Talhah and was slow, and it was never outrun after that. And Hammad ibn Salamah and others reported it."
"6863","6860 - Ahmad ibn Abdah and Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: This verse was revealed: And you concealed within yourself what Allah was to disclose, concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh. This is among what Hammad ibn Zayd alone reported from Thabit from Anas."
"6864","6861 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give a wedding feast for any of his wives as he feasted for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."
"6865","6862 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow perfume on Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf and said: What is this? Or: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman for the weight of a date-pit of gold. He said: May Allah bless you; give a wedding feast even with a sheep."
"6866","6863 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated it to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and established brotherhood among his Companions; he joined Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf with Sad ibn ar-Rabi. Sad said to him: O my brother, I am among the wealthiest people of Madinah, so come and I will share my wealth with you; and I have two wives, I will give up whichever of them you wish for you. Abd ar-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless your family and wealth for you; show me the market. So he showed him the market, and he bought and sold, and he stayed away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for some days. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him with a trace of yellow perfume on his garment and said: What is this? He said: I married a woman. He said: For how much? He said: For the weight of a date-pit of gold. He said: May Allah bless you; give a wedding feast even with a sheep."
"6867","6864 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that he was asked about the dyeing of the hair of the Messenger of Allah. He said: If I wished I could count his gray hairs. And he mentioned that he did not dye, but Abu Bakr and Umar did; Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and Umar dyed with henna alone."
"6868","6865 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once called for water, and a wide shallow bowl was brought. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in it, and the people began performing ablution, and we estimated them between ninety and a hundred; and I kept looking at the water as if springing from between his fingers. And Hammad ibn Salamah also reported it."
"6869","6866 - Ahmad ibn Abdah and Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Thabit, I think from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever raises two daughters, or three, or two sisters or three, until they separate or he dies leaving them, I and he will be in Paradise like these two; and Hammad joined his index and middle fingers. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"6870","6867 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I was in the house of Abu Talhah, and he mentioned a group of Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day wine was prohibited; their drink that day was only fadikh made of unripe and ripe dates. A caller called out, so some of the people said: Go out and see what he says. So I went out, and there was the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announcing: Wine has been prohibited. So it was poured out in the streets of Madinah. I said to Abu Talhah: What do you say? He said: Pour it out, so I poured it out. Hammad said: I do not know whether this is part of the hadith or Thabit said it: His companions said to him: So-and-so was killed on the day of Badr and so-and-so while it was in their stomachs. So Allah revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds."
"6871","6868 - Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratis narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When something was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: Take it to the house of so-and-so woman, for she was a friend of Khadijah. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"6872","6869 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: No two persons love one another for Allah except that the better of them is the one with stronger love for his companion."
"6873","6870 - I found in my book, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Thabit, from Anas; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this chapter, meaning Say: He is Allah, One. He said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Mubarak."
"6874","6871 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: On the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, everything in it was illuminated; and on the day he died, everything in it was darkened; and we had not yet shaken our hands from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were burying him before we felt our hearts had changed. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"6875","6872 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the Ansar; when he came to the homes of the Ansar, the children of the Ansar would gather around him, and he would supplicate for them, wipe their heads, and greet them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the door of Sad and greeted them: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Sad responded but did not let the Prophet hear, until he greeted three times; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not exceed three greetings: if permission was given, otherwise he would leave. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and Sad came hurrying and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One Who sent you with the truth, I heard every greeting you gave and responded to you, but I wanted you to increase greetings and mercy upon us. Enter, O Messenger of Allah. So he entered and sat, and Sad brought food near, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it. When he wanted to leave, he said: May the righteous eat your food, may fasting people break fast with you, and may the angels send blessings upon you. This hadith was reported by Jafar ibn Sulayman and Mamar from Thabit from Anas."
"6876","6873 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Rain befell us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and uncovered his garment until it touched him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do this? He said: It has recently come from its Lord. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"6877","6874 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, and I think from Anas, he said: A man from the Ansar was ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him and met him in the market. He greeted him and said to him: How are you, so-and-so? He said: Well, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I hope in Allah and fear my sins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two do not combine in the heart of a servant in this situation except that Allah gives him what he hopes and secures him from what he fears. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"6878","6875 - Muhanna ibn Yahya al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, he would break it with dates or fresh dates; and if there were none, he would sip some sips of water. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar ibn Sulayman, and we do not know of anyone reporting it from Jafar except Abd ar-Razzaq."
"6879","6876 - Sulayman ibn Abdullah al-Ghaylani narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each of you ask his Lord for his need, or all his needs, even asking Him for his sandal strap when it breaks, and even asking Him for salt. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"6880","6877 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, Abdullah ibn Rawahah walked before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying poetry; Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, before the Messenger of Allah and in the Sanctuary of Allah you speak poetry? He said: Leave him, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, this is harsher upon them than the striking of swords. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar ibn Sulayman, and az-Zuhri reported it from Anas."
"6881","6878 - Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas."
"6882","6879 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer."
"6883","6880 - Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go on expeditions with Umm Sulaym and women with her, and they would give water and treat the wounded."
"6884","6881 - I heard some of our companions, called Abu Zayd al-Ubulli, mention from Yahya ibn Abi Yahya, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on a road, and a black woman passed, and a man said to her: Make way. She said: The road is wide for him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her, for she is strong-willed."
"6885","6882 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah has promised a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him; and whoever He has promised punishment for a deed, He has the choice concerning him."
"6886","6883 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us; and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated it to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, they said: Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah recited to us: He is the Worthy of piety and the Worthy of forgiveness. He said: Your Lord said: I am Worthy of piety, so no partner is associated with Me; and I am Worthy, for whoever fears Me and does not associate with Me, to forgive him; and Abu Qutaybah said in his hadith: Whoever fears Me and does not place a partner with Me, I am Worthy to forgive him."
"6887","6884 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah recited this verse: Those who say: Our Lord is Allah, then remain steadfast. He said: The people have said it, then most of them disbelieved; so whoever says it until he dies upon it is among those who remained steadfast. The hadiths of Suhayl we do not know of anyone reporting them from Thabit except him."
"6888","6886 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Rayyan dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: How did you get these dates? They said: We had low-quality rain-fed dates, so we sold two measures for one. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it to its owner. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Kathir ibn Yasar."
"6889","6887 - Bishr ibn Adam and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, they said: Ad-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Mastur ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left no need nor desire unfulfilled. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: Then this will overcome that. We do not know of Mastur ibn Abbad reporting from Thabit from Anas except this hadith."
"6890","6888 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, meaning as-Sawwaf, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets are alive in their graves praying. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except al-Mustalim ibn Said, and we do not know of al-Hajjaj reporting from Thabit except this hadith."
"6891","6889 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together. We do not know of Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr reporting from Thabit from Anas except this hadith, and Ibn Abi Layla reported it from Thabit from Anas."
"6892","6890 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sadaqah, meaning Ibn Musa, informed us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best fasting. He said: The best fasting is the fasting of Shaban in veneration of Ramadan, and the best charity is charity in Ramadan. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Sadaqah ibn Musa."
"6893","6891 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Nasr narrated to us, Sadaqah, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father died without performing the Hajj of Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think, if your father had a debt would you settle it for him? He said: Yes. He said: Then it is a debt upon him, so settle it. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Sadaqah ibn Musa, and he is a man of Basra against whom there is no harm; his hadith has been accepted, but he was not followed in these two hadiths from Thabit, and we do not know of him reporting from Thabit other than them."
"6894","6892 - Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ammi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah would often say: Are you unable to be like Abu Damdam? They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is Abu Damdam? He said: He was a man before us; when morning came he would say: O Allah, I give my honor in charity against whoever wrongs me. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ammi, a man of Basra who narrated from Thabit and from Ali ibn Zayd."
"6895","6893 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Muslim, the companion of as-Sabiri, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain: it bends at times and stands straight at times."
"6896","6894 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad at-Taymi and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah entered the mosque, no one would raise his head toward him out of awe for him except Abu Bakr and Umar, for he would smile at them and they would smile at him. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah."
"6897","6895 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They name them Muhammad, then they insult them?! This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, and he is a man of Basra against whom there is no harm; he narrated from Thabit, and he alone reported these two hadiths."
"6898","6896 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yahya al-Abahh informed us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my nation is like rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Hammad ibn Yahya, and he was not strong, though the early scholars narrated from him."
"6899","6897 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, and I saw elsewhere: he married her for goods and a hand-mill worth forty dirhams."
"6900","6898 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sawwar Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad over a detachment of cavalry. When he returned to him he said: How did you find it? He said: I saw them rising and falling until I thought I was not suited; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is how it is. Al-Miqdad said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will never work in an official post again. They would say to him: Come forward and lead us in prayer, but he would refuse. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Sawwar Abu Hamzah, and Sawwar was not strong, though many scholars narrated from him."
"6901","6899 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Seven hundred camels belonging to Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf came carrying all kinds of goods, and the people of Madinah were amazed. Aishah said: What is this? They said: A caravan of Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf carrying everything. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I saw Abd ar-Rahman, and he will enter Paradise crawling. That reached him, so he said: O Aishah, what report reached me? She mentioned it to him, so he said: I call you to witness that they, with their saddles, saddle-cloths and loads, are in the path of Allah. This hadith I do not know of anyone reporting it except Umarah from Thabit."
"6902","6900 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated it to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the angel of rain sought permission to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day he said to Umm Salamah: O Umm Salamah, see who is at the door; let no one enter upon us until he leaves. Then al-Husayn came and entered, jumping upon the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began kissing him tenderly. He said: Do you love him? He said: Yes. He said: Your nation will kill him; and if you wish I will show you the place where they will kill him. So he clenched his fist, and there was red soil. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Umarah ibn Zadham."
"6903","6901 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The forerunners are four: I am the forerunner of the Arabs, Salman is the forerunner of Persia, Bilal is the forerunner of Abyssinia, and Suhayb is the forerunner of Rome. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Umarah ibn Zadham."
"6904","6902 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see those who praise extravagantly, throw dust in their faces. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Umarah, nor from Umarah except Muammal ibn Ismail."
"6905","6903 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, did you do such-and-such? He said: No, by the One besides Whom there is no god, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he had done it. He repeated it several times, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been expiated for you by your affirming: There is no god but Allah. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except al-Harith ibn Ubayd Abu Qudamah; Hammad ibn Salamah differed from him and reported it from Thabit from Ibn Umar."
"6906","6904 - Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are with you in one state, but when we leave you we are in another. He said: How are you with your Lord? They said: Allah is our Lord in secret and in public. He said: That is not hypocrisy. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except al-Harith ibn Ubayd."
"6907","6905 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn ash-Shahid narrated to us, Yasar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a slave be led between two men. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Muhammad, nor from Muhammad except Yasar ibn Muhammad."
"6908","6906 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Talhah: Convey peace to your people, and inform them that, as far as I know them, they are chaste and patient."
"6909","6907 - Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Muhammad ibn Thabit."
"6910","6908 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Abd as-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pass by the meadows of Paradise, graze. They said: What are the meadows of Paradise? He said: The circles of remembrance. This hadith was reported from Thabit by Muhammad ibn Thabit and al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, so we sufficed with Muhammad ibn Thabit."
"6911","6909 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd as-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel never ceased enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. This hadith we do not know to be reported from Anas except through this channel, and we do not know of anyone reporting it from Muhammad ibn Thabit except Abd as-Samad."
"6912","6910 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd as-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Muhammad ibn Thabit except Abd as-Samad."
"6913","6911 - I found in my book in my handwriting, from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami: Yasar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Anas; that Umar ibn al-Khattab came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, what prevents you from marrying Fatimah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He will not marry her to me. He said: If he does not marry her to you, to whom will he marry her? You are among the dearest people to him and foremost in Islam. So Abu Bakr went to Aishah and said: O Aishah, if you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in good spirits and turning toward you, mention to him that I mentioned Fatimah; perhaps Allah will make her easy for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and she saw good spirits and attention from him, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr mentioned Fatimah and commanded me to mention her to you. He said: Until the decree descends. So Abu Bakr returned to her, and she said: O my father, I wish I had not mentioned to him what you mentioned. Then Abu Bakr met Umar and mentioned to Umar what Aishah had told him. So Umar went to Hafsah and said: O Hafsah, if you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attentive to you, mention me to him and mention Fatimah to him; perhaps Allah will make her easy for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Hafsah, and she saw his good spirits and attention, so she mentioned Fatimah to him. He said: Until the decree descends. Then Umar met Hafsah and she said: O my father, I wish I had not mentioned anything to him. So Umar went to Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: What prevents you regarding Fatimah? He said: I fear he will not marry her to me. He said: If he does not marry her to you, to whom will he marry her? You are the closest of Allahs creation to him. So Ali went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though he had none like Aishah nor like Hafsah. He met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I wish to marry Fatimah. He said: Do so. He said: I have nothing except my perfumed armor. He said: Gather what you can and bring it to me. So he brought twelve ounces, four hundred and eighty, and brought them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he married Fatimah to him. He took three handfuls and gave them to Umm Ayman, saying: Set aside a handful for perfume, and the rest for what befits a woman of household goods. When she finished preparing and lodged them in a house, he said: O Ali, do not approach your wife until I come to you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them, with Fatimah veiled and Ali sitting and Umm Ayman in the house. He said: O Umm Ayman, bring me a cup of water. She brought him a bowl with water; he drank from it, then spat into it, then handed it to Fatimah, and she drank from it; he took some of it and struck her forehead, between her shoulders and her chest with it. Then he handed it to Ali and said: O Ali, drink. Then he took some of it and struck his forehead and between his shoulders with it. Then he said: My household, may He remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Umm Ayman went out, saying: O Ali, your wife. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Muhammad ibn Thabit, nor from Muhammad except Yasar ibn Muhammad."
"6914","6912 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Badr narrating from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in a circle and wanted to stand, so a boy stood and handed him his sandals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You sought the pleasure of your Lord; may Allah be pleased with you. That boy attained standing in Madinah until he was martyred."
"6915","6913 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Badr narrating from Thabit, from Anas; a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I commit sins. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you sin, seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said: I seek forgiveness, then I return and sin. He said: When you sin, return and seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said: I seek forgiveness, then I return and sin. He said: When you sin, return and seek forgiveness from your Lord. He said it a fourth time, then he said: Seek forgiveness from your Lord until Satan is the one exhausted. These two hadiths we do not know to be reported from Anas except through this channel."
"6916","6914 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani say: I was with Anas ibn Malik, and he had a daughter with him. A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, do you have any need of women? His daughter said: How little is her modesty, or a phrase like it. He said: She is better than you; she desired the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Marhum, and Marhum is a well-known man of Basra."
"6917","6915 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani narrating from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say on the day of the Trench: By Allah, were it not for Allah we would not have been guided, nor fasted nor prayed; so send down tranquility upon us."
"6918","6916 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, and al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah and family there, and I wish to go to them; am I free if I speak ill of you or say something? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He came to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather for me whatever you have, for I wish to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his Companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth seized. This spread in Makkah; the Muslims were dejected and the polytheists displayed joy. The news reached al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he sat in his gathering unable to stand. Mamar said: Uthman al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, he said: Al-Abbas took a son of his called Qutham who resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), lay back and placed him upon his chest, saying: My beloved Qutham, resembling the one with the prominent nose, a prophet of blessings, despite those who are spiteful. Mamar said: Thabit said, from Anas: Then he sent to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat, saying: Woe to you, what have you brought? Al-Hajjaj said to his servant: Convey peace to Abu al-Fadl and tell him: Let him be alone with his son in one of his houses, for the matter is as he would be pleased. His servant came, and when he reached the door he said: Glad tidings, Abu al-Fadl. Al-Abbas leapt joyfully and kissed between his eyes. He informed him of what al-Hajjaj said, and he embraced him. Then al-Hajjaj came and informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar, seized their wealth, the shares of Allah were distributed in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah bint Huyayy for himself, giving her choice between freeing her and being his wife or rejoining her family; she chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for wealth of mine here to gather and take away, so I sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he permitted me to say what I wished; so conceal this from me for three days, then say what you wish. His wife gathered whatever jewelry and goods she had and handed them to him. After three days, al-Abbas came to the wife of al-Hajjaj and said to her: What did al-Hajjaj do? She informed him he had left, saying: Let not what reached you grieve you, Abu al-Fadl. He said: Yes; may Allah not grieve me; by praise of Allah it was only what we loved. Al-Hajjaj informed me that Allah opened Khaybar to His Messenger, the shares of Allah were distributed, and he chose Safiyyah for himself; if you have need of your husband, join him. She said: I think by Allah you are truthful. He said: I am truthful, and the matter is as I told you. Then he went to the gatherings of Quraysh, and they were saying: May only good befall you, Abu al-Fadl. He said: Only good befell me, by praise of Allah. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat informed me that Allah opened Khaybar to His Messenger, the shares of Allah were distributed in it, and he chose Safiyyah for himself; he asked me to conceal it for three days. He only came to take his wealth and whatever he had here, then leave. So Allah turned the dejection that was upon the Muslims onto the polytheists; the Muslims who had entered their houses dejected came out to al-Abbas, and he informed them, so the Muslims rejoiced, and Allah turned what was of dejection and grief onto the polytheists. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Mamar."
"6919","6917 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas."
"6920","6918 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, and the wording is that of Zuhayr, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged the women, he took upon them that they not wail. They said: O Messenger of Allah, women assisted us in the pre-Islamic period; shall we assist them in Islam? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no assisting in wailing in Islam, nor shighar marriage in Islam, nor jilab, nor junub; and whoever plunders is not of us. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Mamar."
"6921","6919 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, they said: Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas; that al-Mughirah ibn Shubah wished to marry a woman and mentioned it to the Prophet. He said: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you. He did so and married her, and he mentioned her compatibility. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Mamar."
"6922","6920 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I counted on the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only fourteen white hairs."
"6923","6921 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, with the wording of Zuhayr: Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit: that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may intercede for two or three men."
"6924","6922 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: There was a Bedouin man named Zahir ibn Haram, or Ibn Hizam, Abd ar-Razzaq doubted; he would bring gifts to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the desert. The Prophet said: Zahir is our desert-dweller and we, I think he said, are his townsfolk, or his town-dweller. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved him, and he was an unattractive man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind until his back touched his belly. He said: Release me from this. He turned to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Who will buy the slave? He said: O Messenger of Allah, then by Allah you will find me unsellable. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But with Allah you are not unsellable; and he said: But with Allah you are profitable, or a phrase like it. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Mamar."
"6925","6923 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come upon anyone who says: Allah, Allah."
"6926","6924 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty was never in anything except that it adorned it, and obscenity was never in anything except that it disgraced it."
"6927","6925 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed on behalf of Julaybib a woman of the Ansar to her father. He said: Until I consult her mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then yes. The man went to his wife and mentioned it to her. She said: No, by Allah; did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find none but Julaybib, when we refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so? The girl was in her chamber listening. The man and his wife set out intending the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the girl said: Where are you going? Do you wish to reject the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If he is pleased with him for you, then marry him. It was as if a fetter was loosened from her parents, or a phrase like it. They said: You are right. Her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: If you were pleased with him, we are pleased. He said: So he married her. Then the people of Madinah were alarmed for battle; Julaybib rode out and they found him killed, with around him as many polytheists as Allah willed whom he had killed. Anas said: I saw her, and she was among the most charitable widows of Madinah. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Mamar."
"6928","6926 - Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahim, the companion of as-Sabiri, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated it to us, they said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a hadith over which we never rejoiced since knowing Islam as we rejoiced over it. He said: The believer is rewarded for guiding to the path and removing harm from the road; he is rewarded for expressing in his tongue on behalf of the non-Arab; he is rewarded for coming to his wife; even he is rewarded for a commodity at the edge of his garment which he feels, ties its place, or a phrase like it, so his heart throbs for it, then Allah returns it to him and records its reward for him. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, and al-Minhal is trustworthy."
"6929","6927 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: We were forbidden in the Quran from asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we liked that an intelligent Bedouin man come and ask him while we listened. A Bedouin man came and said: Our messenger came to us informing us that you claim Allah sent you. He said: He spoke truth. He said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah. He said: Who created the earth? He said: Allah. He said: Who erected the mountains? He said: Allah. He said: Who placed benefits in them? He said: Allah. He said: By the One Who created the heaven and created the earth and erected the mountains therein and placed benefits therein, did Allah send you? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed we must pray five prayers each day and night. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed we must give charity from our wealth. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed we must fast a month in our year. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed we must perform Hajj to the House for whoever can find a way. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? He said: Yes. He said: By the One Who sent you, I will neither add anything to them nor subtract anything from them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise. This hadith we do not know of anyone completing its wording from Thabit from Anas better than Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah; others reported it, and Sulayman was among the trustworthy of Basra."
"6930","6928 - Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahim narrated to us, Abu an-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the morning prayer, people would come with their vessels, or a vessel with water, for him to dip his hand in, seeking the blessing of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); sometimes they would come on a cold morning and he would dip his hand in it."
"6931","6929 - Amr ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked away from a riding companion of his. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi, called at-Tall, a trustworthy Kufan."
"6932","6930 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: A boy was born to me tonight and I named him after my father Ibrahim; then I entrusted him to a woman called Umm Sayf, the wife of a smith called Abu Yusuf. He set out and I followed him until we reached Abu Yusuf; the house was full. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the child and embraced him and said what Allah willed him to say. Anas said: I saw him struggling with himself; the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears, and he said: The eye weeps and the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord; by Allah, O Ibrahim, we are grieved by you. Abu Bakr said: This is my retention from Abu Musa, from Abu Amir, or something like this."
"6933","6931 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Mani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon young men of Quraysh and said: O company of youths, whoever among you can afford provision, let him marry; otherwise, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit except Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah."
"6934","6932 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend a journey, so provide me. He said: May Allah provide you with piety. He said: Increase for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And forgive your sin. He said: Increase for me, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And direct you to good wherever you are. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Jafar."
"6935","6933 - Al-Abbas ibn Jafar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Bishr, called Ibn al-Muzalliq, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at night, he would clean himself, perform ablution, use the tooth-stick, then send seeking perfume among the rooms of his wives."
"6936","6934 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated it to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Harashi narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, and he was trustworthy, he said: from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has servants who recognize people by marks. These two hadiths we do not know of anyone reporting them from Thabit from Anas except Abu Bishr."
"6937","6935 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not commit sins, I would fear for you what is greater than that: self-admiration. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, and he is a well-known man from whom Affan and the early scholars reported."
"6938","6936 - Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes. He said: The best of you in conduct, or he said: the best of you in character. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Suhayl."
"6939","6937 - Isa ibn Musa as-Sami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Kinanah ibn Jabalah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Adam prostrates, Satan says: The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate and prostrated, so Paradise is his; and I was commanded to prostrate but disobeyed, so the Fire is mine, or similar speech. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Suhayl except Kinanah ibn Jabalah, and we do not know it reported from Anas through other than this channel, and it is strange from Anas."
"6940","6938 - Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi and Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Abbad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was pleased with a man in some manner, would command him to pray."
"6941","6939 - Al-Abbas ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Zafar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Paradise? He said: Whoever does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves. It was said: Who are the people of Hell? He said: Whoever does not die until his ears are filled with what he hates. Thus I found it with Abbas, and we do not know of anyone reporting this hadith from Anas except Thabit, nor from Thabit except Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah."
"6942","6940 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Salih ibn Bashir al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who frequent the houses of Allah are the people of Allah. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Salih."
"6943","6941 - Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Jafar ibn Zayd and Mansur ibn Zadham, from Anas ibn Malik, raising it, he said: An angel is entrusted with the Scale; the son of Adam is brought and stood between the two pans of the Scale. If his scale is heavy, an angel calls with a voice heard by all creation: So-and-so is happy with a happiness after which he will never be wretched. If the scale is light, an angel calls with a voice heard by all creation: So-and-so is wretched with a wretchedness after which he will never be happy. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Thabit from Anas except Salih al-Murri, nor from Jafar except Salih."
"6944","6942 - Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Malik narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah; I think he said: So let not Allah seek from you anything of His protection."
"6945","6943 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of our youths is one who resembles our elders, and the worst of our elders is one who resembles our youths."
"6946","6944 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, I think he said, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"6947","6945 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi as-Sahba narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Barirah was a slave-girl and was freed, then charity was given to her; some of that charity was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, it is from what was given in charity to Barirah. He said: For her it is charity, and for us a gift."
"6948","6946 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Laythi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Creation are the dependents of Allah, and the most beloved of them to Allah are the most beneficial to His dependents."
"6949","6947 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Laythi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met a man called Harithah in one of the streets of Madinah and said: How did you wake, O Harithah? He said: I woke as a true believer. He said: Every faith has a reality; what is the reality of your faith? He said: My soul turned away from this world, so I thirsted and kept my night sleepless; it is as if I see the Throne of my Lord manifest, and as if I see the people of Paradise enjoying in Paradise and the people of Hell being punished in Hell. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have hit right, so remain firm; a believer whose heart Allah has illuminated."
"6950","6948 - With his chain; he said: A man known for worship and striving was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: How does your companion remember death? They said: We do not hear him mention it. He said: Then your companion is not there. These hadiths we do not know of anyone reporting them from Thabit from Anas except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah, and he is weak in hadith though people narrated from him."
"6951","6949 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Tamim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Jafar ar-Razi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are: Maryam daughter of Imran, Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh, Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid, and Fatimah daughter of Muhammad. Abu Bakr said: This is not with us in Basra."
"6952","6950 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us, ad-Dahhak ibn Nibras, against whom there is no harm, narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with his Companions, a man in travel clothes came to him, threading through the people until he sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted; he placed his hand upon the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, what is Islam? He said: Testifying there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; establishing prayer; giving charity; fasting the month of Ramadan; and pilgrimage to the House if you can find a way to it. He said: If I do that, am I a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke truth. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look, he asks him yet confirms him, as if he knows more than him, and they did not know the man. Then he said: O Muhammad, what is faith? He said: Faith in Allah, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, the prophets, death, resurrection, reckoning, Paradise, Hell, and the decree, all of it. He said: If I do that, am I a believer? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke truth. He said: O Muhammad, what is excellence? He said: To fear Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, am I excellent? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke truth. He said: O Muhammad, when is the Hour? He said: The one asked about it knows no more than the asker. The man turned away and left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Bring me the man. They followed seeking him but saw nothing. They returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we followed the man seeking him but saw nothing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That was Gabriel; he came to teach you your religion. This hadith we do not know to be reported from Anas except through this channel with this chain; ad-Dahhak ibn Nibras reported more than one hadith from Thabit, there is no harm in him, though strange among the hadith of Anas."
"6953","6951 - Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded with the tooth-stick until I feared I would become toothless, or until I feared for my gums and teeth."
"6954","6952 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Hassan ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah: When fresh dates come, congratulate me. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it except Hassan ibn Siyah from Thabit from Anas, and he reported from Thabit from Anas other hadiths not followed in."
"6955","6953 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid an-Narsi narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on Friday when the people rose, saying: O Messenger of Allah, rain has failed, souls are strained, livestock perished; supplicate to Allah to give us water. He said: By Allah, we saw no patch of cloud in the sky; then a cloud formed and spread, then it rained. He said: They were rained upon until the next Friday. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood delivering the sermon, they said: O Messenger of Allah, houses collapsed and roads were cut; supplicate to Allah to withhold it from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. It cleared from Madinah, and rain fell around Madinah but not upon it. This hadith has been reported from Thabit through various channels, and we do not know of anyone reporting it from Ubaydullah from Thabit from Anas with similar wording."
"6956","6954 - Ismail ibn Ishaq and Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Yunus, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6957","6955 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, Amr ibn Rudayh narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. None reported this hadith from Yunus except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"6958","6956 - Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us from his book, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit, from Anas; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not done deeds like theirs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with the one he loves. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Yunus except Khalid ibn Abdullah, though it has been reported from Thabit by more than one."
"6959","6957 - Al-Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us, Shabbah ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night when half the night had passed, or nearly half; he said: I kept looking at the glitter of his ring in his hand. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Yunus except Shabbah ibn Zayd, and he is the father of Umar ibn Shabbah."
"6960","6958 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When wine was prohibited, we poured it out with nothing in it. This hadith we do not know of anyone reporting it from Yunus except Abu Shihab."
"6961","6960 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he placed me at his right. And this hadith was narrated by others than Yahya ibn Isma'il from Hushaym from Yunus, from Thabit saying: I prayed with Anas and he placed me at his right. And no one raised it except Yahya."
"6962","6961 - Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The expiation of the gathering is that you say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this channel, and Uthman ibn Matar is lenient in hadith, and Muslim and others narrated from him."
"6963","6962 - Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Abu Raja al-Kalbi Rawh ibn al-Musayyib - trustworthy - narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The women came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the virtue and jihad in the path of Allah, so what deed is there for us by which we may attain the deed of the mujahidin in the path of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you remains - or a word like it - in her house, she attains the deed of the mujahid in the path of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit except Rawh ibn al-Musayyib, and he is a well-known man from the people of Basrah."
"6964","6963 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Khazraj ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Thabit except al-Khazraj ibn Uthman."
"6965","6964 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us - he died recently in the year two hundred, and he is trustworthy - Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq, and it is a white animal, above the donkey and below the mule, placing its hoof at the edge of its sight. He said: So I rode it and it went with me until I came to the gate of Bayt al-Maqdis, and I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie. He said: Then I entered the mosque and prayed in it two rak'ahs, then I came out, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me with a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk, and I chose the milk, so Jibril said: You have hit upon the fitrah. Then he took us up to the lowest heaven, and Jibril, peace be upon him, asked for it to be opened, and it was said: And who are you? He said: I am Jibril. And it was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. He said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. He said: So it was opened for us, and there I was with Adam, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the second heaven, and Jibril asked for it to be opened. It was said: Who are you? He said: I am Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. He said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. He said: So it was opened for us, and there I was with the two sons of the maternal aunt, Isa and Yahya, and they welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the third heaven, and Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Yusuf, and he had been given half of beauty, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the fourth, and Jibril asked for it to be opened. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. He said: So it was opened for us, and there I was with Idris, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted says: And We raised him to a high station. He said: Then he took us up to the fifth heaven, and Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. He said: So it was opened for us, and there I was with Harun, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the sixth heaven, and Jibril asked for it to be opened. It was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) It was said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Musa, peace be upon him, and he welcomed me and supplicated good. Then he took us up to the seventh heaven, and Jibril asked for it to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: And has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. So it was opened for us, and there I was with Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and he was leaning against al-Bayt al-Ma'mur, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me, and seventy thousand angels enter it - meaning al-Bayt al-Ma'mur - then they do not return to it. Then he took me to Sidrat al-Muntaha, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants, and its fruits like large jars. When there covered it of the command of Allah what covered it, it changed, and no one of Allah's creation can describe it for its beauty. So He revealed to me what He revealed, and obligated upon me fifty prayers in every day and night. So I descended until I reached Musa, and he said: What did your Lord obligate upon your ummah? I said: Fifty prayers in every day and night. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening, for your ummah cannot bear that, and I have tested the Children of Isra'il and experienced them. He said: So I returned to my Lord the Blessed and Exalted, and said: My Lord, lighten for my ummah. So He removed five from me. He said: Then I returned to Musa, and he said: What did you do? I said: He removed five from me. He said: Your ummah cannot bear that, so return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening for your ummah. I kept returning between my Lord and Musa, He removing five, until He said: O Muhammad, they are five prayers in every day and night, with every prayer ten, so those are fifty prayers. And whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him; if he does it, ten are written for him. And whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, nothing is written; if he does it, one evil deed is written. He said: So I descended until I reached Musa, peace be upon him, and informed him of that, and he said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for lightening. I said: I have returned to my Lord until I am ashamed."
"6966","6965 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: that a comer came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was playing with the boys, so he took him and threw him down, and split his chest, and took out the heart, and split the heart, and took out of it a clot, and said: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then joined it and returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother and said: Muhammad has been killed. She came and met them while he was pale in colour. Anas said: I used to see the trace of the stitching in his chest."
"6967","6966 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the path of Allah, or an evening, is better than the world and what is in it."
"6968","6967 - And with his isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wisal, so some people of his companions performed wisal, so he said: If the month had been extended for me, I would have performed a wisal that those who go deep would leave their deepening; I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"6969","6968 - Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man from the people of Persia, a neighbour of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), had good-smelling broth, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while A'ishah was at his side, and he gestured to him with his hand - meaning: he pointed to him with his hand - and he gestured: me and A'ishah? He said: No. Then he gestured to him, and he gestured to him: me and A'ishah? And he pointed to him: No. Then he gestured to him, and he gestured: Then yes, so he came to us. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6970","6969 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went to his bed said: Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink and sheltered us; how many are there who have neither one to suffice them nor shelter."
"6971","6970 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while Abdullah ibn Salam was in his date-palms; when he heard of him he came and said: O Muhammad, I am asking you about things that none knows except a prophet; if you inform me of them then you are the Messenger of Allah. So he asked him about resemblance, and about the first thing that will gather the people, and about the first thing the people of Paradise will eat? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril informed me of them just now. Abdullah said: He is the enemy of the Jews. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for resemblance: if the fluid of the man precedes the fluid of the woman, it takes the resemblance, and if the fluid of the woman precedes the fluid of the man, she takes the resemblance. And as for the first thing that will gather the people: a fire coming from the direction of the east, gathering the people to the west. And the first thing the people of Paradise will eat is the extra lobe of the liver of the fish. So Ibn Salam believed and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people, and if they hear of my Islam they will slander me and speak against me, so hide me and send for them, and ask them about me. So he sent for them and they came - and he had hidden him - and said: What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you? They said: Our chief and the son of our chief, and our best and the son of our best, and our scholar and the son of our scholar. He said: What would you think if he believed, would you believe? They said: May Allah protect him from that; he would not do it. He said: Come out, O Ibn Salam, to them. So he came out and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. They said: Rather he is the worst of us and the son of the worst of us, and our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one. He said: Did I not tell you, O Messenger of Allah, that they are a slanderous people?"
"6972","6971 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raid at the time of the Fajr prayer, and he would listen; if he heard an adhan he held back, otherwise he raided. One day he listened and heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitrah. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. So he said: You have come out of the Fire."
"6973","6972 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when Ruqayyah died: No man who approached his wife last night shall enter the grave. So Uthman did not enter. The common people do not narrate this."
"6974","6973 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a market in which there are dunes of musk; they come to it every Friday, and a north wind blows, scattering upon their faces and their clothes and their houses, so they increase in beauty and loveliness. They return to their families having increased in beauty and loveliness, and their families say to them: You have increased in beauty and loveliness. And they say: And you too have increased in beauty and loveliness."
"6975","6974 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a woman in whose intellect was something said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He said: O mother of so-and-so, see which road you wish, and he stayed with her until she fulfilled her need."
"6976","6975 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Who will take this sword? Then he said: With its right. The people held back, so Abu Dujanah took it, and he used to cut with it the heads of the polytheists."
"6977","6976 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was frightened in Allah, and no one is frightened; and I was harmed in Allah, and no one is harmed."
"6978","6977 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us - and the wording is Muhammad's - they said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that Safiyyah fell in the share of Dihyah al-Kalbi, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought her for seven heads."
"6979","6978 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, the Ansar have taken all the reward; we never saw people better in giving for much, nor better in sharing in little than them, and they sufficed us the burden and shared with us in the pleasant outcome. He said: Do you not praise them for it and supplicate for them? They said: Yes. He said: Then that is for that."
"6980","6979 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the people of Yemen came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Send with us a man to teach us. So he took the hand of Abu Ubaydah and sent him with them, and said: This is the trustworthy one of this ummah."
"6981","6980 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until none says on earth: Allah, Allah, and until the sky rains and the earth does not grow, and until there is for fifty women one caretaker, and until a woman passes by a sandal and says: It once had a man."
"6982","6981 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: that a young man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to equip myself and I have nothing with which to equip myself. He said: Go to so-and-so, for he had equipped himself and fallen sick. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveys salam to you, and says: Hand over to me what you equipped. He said that to him, and he said: O so-and-so, give him what you equipped me with, and do not withhold anything from him, for by Allah if you withhold anything from him it will not be blessed for you."
"6983","6982 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that eighty men of the people of Makkah came down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions from above the mountain from the direction of al-Tan'im to kill them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took them peacefully and freed them. So Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent down: And He is the One who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them, until the end of the verse."
"6984","6983 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that al-Adba could not be beaten, then one day a Bedouin came on a young camel of his and raced her, and beat her. That was hard upon the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and broke them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is indeed a right upon Allah the Blessed and Exalted that nothing of the world is raised except He lowers it."
"6985","6984 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of Banu al-Najjar, and said: O maternal uncle, say: There is no god but Allah. He said: Maternal uncle or paternal uncle? He said: Rather maternal uncle. He said: And is it better for me to say it? He said: Yes."
"6986","6985 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"6987","6986 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah the Blessed and Exalted fashioned Adam, He left him as long as Allah willed to leave him, and Iblis began circling around him; when he saw him hollow he knew that he has no self-control."
"6988","6987 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a gathering while they were laughing, and said: Increase in remembrance of the destroyer of pleasures - I think he said - for no one remembers it in straitened livelihood except it widens it for him, nor in ease except it straitens it for him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Hammad ibn Salamah except Mu'ammal."
"6989","6988 - Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that two brothers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one of them used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the other used to earn a living, so the earning one complained of his brother to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Perhaps you are only provided for because of him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Hammad except Abu Dawud."
"6990","6989 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The most favoured of people in the world will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and He will say: Dip him a dipping in the Fire. Then he will be brought and He will say: O son of Adam, did you ever attain any bliss? He will say: No, by Your might, I never saw any good, nor any joy, nor any delight of the eye. He said: And the most severely afflicted of people in trial and harm and hardship will be brought and He will say: Dip him a dipping in Paradise. So he will be dipped in it, then brought and He will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see any misery or anything you dislike? He will say: No, by Your might, I never saw anything I dislike. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6991","6990 - Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by night by Musa ibn Imran, peace be upon him, while he was praying in his grave."
"6992","6991 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw tonight as if I were in the house of Uqbah ibn Rafi', and we were brought fresh dates of Ibn Tab; I interpreted that as: for us is the world and well-being in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good for us. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit from Anas except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6993","6992 - Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a sound among the date-palms and said: What is this? He said: They are pollinating the date-palms. He said: If they left them they would be fine. So they left them, and they became poor dates. They informed him of that, so he said: You know better what benefits you in your world; as for the matter of your Hereafter, it is to me. None narrated it except Hammad."
"6994","6993 - And with his isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Abu Ubaydah and Abu Talhah."
"6995","6994 - And with his isnad, and Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to deliver the khutbah leaning on a trunk of a date-palm; when the minbar was made he moved to it, and it moaned. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until he embraced it, and it calmed. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"6996","6995 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Jews used to isolate women in menstruation, neither eating with them nor drinking with them, and expelling them from houses. So there came down: And they ask you about menstruation; say: It is harm, so keep away from women in menstruation. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to eat with them and drink with them, and to do everything except intercourse. The Jews said: Muhammad does not want to leave anything of our affair except he opposes us in it. So Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews say such-and-such, so if you permitted us intercourse with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry at that with severe anger, until we thought he had found against them both because of that. They left, then milk was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, and they came, and he gave them to drink of that milk, so we knew he had not found against them. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, and it is a hadith in which Hammad is alone, and we do not know of anyone narrating it other than Hammad, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Hammad from Thabit and Asim except Amr ibn Asim."
"6997","6996 - al-Husayn ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: Feed food, and spread salam, and speak good words, and pray at night while people sleep; you will enter Paradise in peace. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit from Anas except Hafs ibn Aslam, and he narrated from Thabit other than one hadith."
"6998","6997 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ma'bad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jammaz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love of Quraysh is faith, and hatred of them is disbelief; whoever loves the Arabs has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit except al-Haytham ibn Jammaz, and al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated something like it, and al-Hasan and al-Haytham - their hadith is not used as proof when the hadith is alone."
"6999","6998 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a vessel of a little water was brought, and the water began gushing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7000","6999 - I found in my book from Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this surah, meaning: Say: He is Allah, One. He said: Your love of it has admitted you to Paradise."
"7001","7000 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam Abu Badr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A single trait in a man by which Allah rectifies all his deed, and a man's purification for his prayer by which Allah expiates his sins and his prayer remains for him as supererogatory."
"7002","7001 - And with his isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abu Dharr and said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to two traits, light upon the back and heavier in the scale than others? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Upon you is good character and long silence; by the One in whose hand is my soul, the creatures never did anything like them. And the two hadiths of Bashshar ibn al-Hakam, we do not know of anyone narrating them other than him from Thabit."
"7003","7002 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Habib al-Laythi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness was never in anything except it adorned it, nor was harshness in anything except it disgraced it, and Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness. And this hadith, Ma'mar narrated part of it from Thabit, and Kathir ibn Habib added in it an addition which we mentioned for that."
"7004","7003 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hibban ibn Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of the rich of my ummah to enter Paradise is Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he will not enter it except crawling."
"7005","7004 - And with his isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The treacherous imam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and the subjects will dispute against him and prevail over him, and it will be said to him: Fill a corner of the corners of Hell. And the two hadiths of Aghlab ibn Tamim, we do not know of anyone narrating them from him except his son, nor do we know of them being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this channel with this isnad, and Aghlab is not a preserver."
"7006","7005 - And with his isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Say: He is Allah, One two hundred times, Allah removes from him the sins of two hundred years. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Thabit except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far and Aghlab ibn Tamim, and they are close in poor memory, and al-Hasan is more famous and more understanding."
"7007","7006 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muslim al-Ijli narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Say: He is Allah, One equals a third of the Quran, and When the earth is shaken equals a fourth of the Quran."
"7008","7007 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Daylam ibn Ghazwan informed us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of his companions to a man of the great ones of Jahiliyyah calling him to Allah the Blessed and Exalted, and he said: What is your Lord to whom you call? Is He of brass? Is He of iron? Is He of silver? Is He of gold? He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him back a second time and he said the like of that. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he sent him to him a third time, and he said the like of that. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent upon him a thunderbolt and burned him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted has sent upon your companion a thunderbolt and burned him. Then this verse came down: And He sends the thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah, and He is severe in assault. Daylam is a righteous Basran."
"7009","7008 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There were orphans in the care of Abu Talhah, and he bought wine for them; when the prohibition of wine came down, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Shall I make it vinegar? He said: No. So he poured it away. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from the hadith of Yahya ibn Ubadah, and al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas, in which Qays said, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, from Abu Talhah."
"7010","7009 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on the road by a date and said: Were it not that I fear it is of charity, I would have eaten it. And we do not know of Talhah ibn Musarrif narrating from Anas except this hadith."
"7011","Qatadah from Anas. 7010 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and they used to open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"7012","7011 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Humayd and Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar used to open the recitation with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And we do not know of Ayyub narrating from Qatadah from Anas except this hadith, nor of Humayd narrating from Qatadah from Anas except two hadiths, this is one of them, and the other is:"
"7013","7012 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he heard the voice of a mu'adhdhin saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. So he said: He was sincere. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: He has come out of disbelief. He said: Then we looked and he was a shepherd; the prayer came and he gave the adhan, or words like this."
"7014","7013 - Ahmad ibn Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik."
"7015","7014 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from al-Taymi, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until he kept gurgling it, or gurgling with it in his chest, and his tongue could not utter it, and the wording is the wording of al-Mu'tamir. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this channel, nor do we know of anyone corroborating al-Taymi in his narration from Qatadah from Anas, and others than al-Taymi narrate it from Qatadah from Salih Abu al-Khalil from Safinah from Umm Salamah."
"7016","7015 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When we returned from al-Hudaybiyah, and we had been kept from our rites, and we were between grief and gloom, Allah the Exalted sent down: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sin, and complete His favour upon you, and guide you to a straight path, or as Allah willed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has been sent down upon me a verse dearer to me than the whole world. And this hadith we mentioned from al-Taymi from Qatadah, because of the eminence of al-Taymi; for al-Taymi narrates from Anas many hadiths."
"7017","7016 - He narrated it to us, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken up by night, there was presented to him a river whose banks were hollowed ruby - or he said: hollowed - and the angel who was with him struck with his hand and took out musk. Muhammad said to the angel who was with him: What is this? He said: Al-Kawthar which Allah gave you. And Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for him, and he saw at it a great matter, or as he said."
"7018","7017 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, in marfu' form: that he mentioned al-Kawthar, he said: So I struck with my hand in it, and there was musk. Then he mentioned the like of it. And this hadith was narrated from Anas and from others than Anas, and this isnad is of the best isnad narrated in that from Anas."
"7019","7018 - And with his first isnad, from Anas: that he narrated - I think - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years and does not cut it, or as he said."
"7020","7019 - And Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated it to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. And Abu Attab narrated it from Sa'id from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Anas, and he erred in it. And Shu'bah narrated it from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know of anyone narrating it from Shu'bah except Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi."
"7021","7020 - Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, Abu Bahr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I repent to Allah in the day a hundred times. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Qatadah from Anas except al-Taymi and Imran al-Qattan."
"7022","As for the hadith of Imran, 7021 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7023","7022 - And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the disbeliever does a good deed he is fed a morsel of the world for it, and as for the believer, Allah delays for him, or stores for him his good deeds in the Hereafter. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Qatadah from Anas except al-Taymi."
"7024","7023 - And with his isnad: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Hudaybiyah: Leave me, so he went with the sacrificial animals and slaughtered them, or as he said - and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said: No, by Allah, we shall not be like the chiefs of the Children of Isra'il when they said to Musa: Go you and your Lord and fight, we are sitting here; but: Go you and your Lord and fight, we are with you fighting. So he slaughtered the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyah. Qatadah said: And there were with them on that day seventy camels. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Qatadah from Anas except from the narration of al-Taymi from Qatadah from Anas."
"7025","7024 - And with his isnad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and He turns to whoever repents."
"7026","7025 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I do not know whether something was sent down or he was saying it: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would wish, or seek, a second valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"7027","7026 - And Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ali ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7028","7027 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"7029","7028 - And with the first isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they asked him until they pressed him with asking. Once he said: Ask me, you will not ask me about anything except I shall explain it to you. The people fell silent and feared that a great matter had come down. Anas said: We began looking right and left, and I saw only every man wrapping his head in his garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Ask me, you will not ask me about anything except I shall explain it to you. A man stood from the side of the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah, and the man's name is Kharijah - when Umar saw that, he stood and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger; we seek refuge with Allah from the evil of trials. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I never saw like today in good and evil; Paradise and the Fire were depicted for me and I saw them below that wall, or as he said."
"7030","7029 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham - meaning Ibn Abi Abdullah - narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they pressed him with asking. One day he ascended the minbar and said: You will not ask me about anything except I shall explain it to you. Anas said: I began looking right and left at every man wrapping his head in his garment, weeping. A man arose who, when he quarrelled with men, was attributed to other than his father, and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Umar arose and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger; we seek refuge with Allah from trials. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I never saw like today in good and evil; Paradise was depicted until I saw it behind this wall. And Qatadah, when he mentioned this hadith, used to recite this verse: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, would grieve you. And this hadith was narrated from Anas from more than one channel, and the hadith of Qatadah from Anas is the most complete in wording."
"7031","7030 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: What is between the two sides of my Hawd is as between Madinah and San'a."
"7032","7031 - And with his isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between his two eyes is written: disbeliever, meaning the Dajjal."
"7033","7032 - And with his isnad, he said: The believers will come to Adam on the Day of Resurrection and say: Allah made His angels prostrate to you, so intercede for us with Allah to relieve us. He will say: I am not there; go to Nuh. They will come to Nuh and he will say: I am not there. They will come to Ibrahim the friend of Allah and he will say: I am not there, but go to Isa, the word of Allah and His spirit. They will come to Isa, and he will say: I am not there; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Allah has forgiven him his former and latter sin. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So they will come to me, and I shall come to my Lord the Blessed and Exalted and ask His permission, and permission will be given to me. When I look at my Lord the Blessed and Exalted I shall fall to Him prostrating, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me, and He will say, or it will be said: Rise, Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, and intercede and you will be granted intercession. So He will set for me a limit, and I shall take them out and admit them to Paradise. Then I shall return to my Lord the Blessed and Exalted a second time, and when I see my Lord I shall fall to Him prostrating, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me, and He will say, or it will be said: Rise, Muhammad, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and you will be granted intercession. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He teaches me, then I shall intercede, and He will set for me a limit, and I shall admit them to Paradise, until I shall say: None remains in the Fire except whom the Quran has held back, or as he said."
"7034","7033 - And Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated it to us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will be gathered and made to perceive that, and they will come to Adam, and he mentioned the like of it. And this hadith was narrated by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Anas also, and we do not know of anyone narrating it from Shu'bah except Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi, and we never heard anyone narrating it from Abu Bahr except Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali."
"7035","7034 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Therein are seen pitchers of gold and silver, the number of the stars of the sky or more, meaning the Hawd."
"7036","7035 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, will he come to Madinah? He said: He will head for it and find the angels guarding it, meaning the Dajjal."
"7037","7036 - And Taliq ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet the like of it. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Shu'bah except Yazid ibn Harun."
"7038","7037 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing."
"7039","7038 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing. And this hadith was narrated from Anas from more than one channel, and this channel is of the best narrated from Anas in that."
"7040","7039 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If I were invited to a trotter I would go, and if it were gifted to me I would accept."
"7041","7040 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah from Anas: that al-Rubayyi' bint al-Nadr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah was struck on the day of Badr while watching; if he is in Paradise I shall be patient and seek reward, and if it is other than that I shall strive in weeping. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are gardens within a garden, and he has attained al-Firdaws al-A'la. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Qatadah from Anas."
"7042","7041 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a Jew for a slave-girl whom he killed for her silver ornaments."
"7043","7042 - And with his isnad: that a man called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday while he was addressing the people in Madinah: O Messenger of Allah, rain has failed, so ask your Lord for rain for us. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked, and there was no trace of a large cloud. So he asked for rain, and the clouds gathered to one another, until the waterways of Madinah flowed. They remained so until the next Friday without ceasing. Then that man, or another, stood while the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have drowned, so supplicate Allah to hold it back from us. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said: O Allah, around us and not upon us; O Allah, around us and not upon us. He smiled twice - or three times. He said: So the clouds began breaking away from Madinah right and left; what is around it is rained upon and nothing in it is rained upon, that Allah may show them the honour of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the answering of his supplication."
"7044","7043 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, the like of it."
"7045","7044 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between his two eyes is written: disbeliever, every believing literate and illiterate reads it, meaning the Dajjal."
"7046","7045 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show them a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."
"7047","7046 - Ahmad ibn Abi Ubaydullah al-Warraq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the striking, or treading, of their sandals. He said: And two angels come to him and sit him up in his grave and say to him: What did you used to say about this man? As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. They say to him: Look at your seat of the Fire, and they show him his seat of Paradise and his seat of the Fire, and he sees them both. And this hadith was narrated by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, and Shayban also narrated the like of it."
"7048","7047 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the striking of their sandals. He said: Two angels come to him and say: What did you used to say about this man? He said: As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. It is said to him: Look at your seat of the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat of Paradise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So he sees them both."
"7049","7048 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid - meaning Ibn Zuray' - narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that there was once an alarm, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse of Abu Talhah which was slow, or in which was slowness. When he returned he said: I found this horse of yours a sea of seas. Afterwards it could not be outrun."
"7050","7049 - And Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, the like of it."
"7051","7050 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to a group and to some people of the non-Arabs, and it was said to him: They do not accept a letter except with a seal upon it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, and I can almost see the glint of the ring on the finger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or in his palm."
"7052","7051 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Yazid ibn Zuray' from Sa'id from Qatadah from Anas other than Amr ibn Ali, nor do we know this hadith from the hadith of Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Anas; rather it is only known from Ma'mar from Qatadah from Anas."
"7053","7052 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and the sons of the Ansar and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. And this hadith, they criticised Amr ibn Ali for it from the hadith of Yazid, and he remained upon it until he died."
"7054","7053 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years and does not cut it, and he recited: And extended shade."
"7055","7054 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? His word about that was severe, and he said: You shall surely stop that, or your sights shall surely be snatched away. And this hadith was narrated by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, and Sa'id ibn Bashir also narrated them both from Qatadah from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7056","7055 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When this verse came down: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sin, on his return from al-Hudaybiyah while grief and gloom mingled with them, he said: There has been sent down upon me a verse dearer to me than the whole world. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know what will be done with you. He said: Then this verse came down: That He may admit the believing men and the believing women, up to His word: mighty."
"7057","7056 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: Indeed We have granted you a clear victory. He said: Al-Hudaybiyah."
"7058","7057 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, from Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not perform wisal. They said: O Prophet of Allah, you perform wisal. He said: I am not like any of you; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"7059","7058 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated it to us, from Abu Dawud, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as far as I know the like of it."
"7060","7059 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam silk shirts because of an itch that was in them."
"7061","7060 - Nasr narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas."
"7062","7061 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la and Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"7063","7062 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Shu'ayb - meaning Ibn al-Habhab - from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and married her, and made her freedom her dowry."
"7064","7063 - And Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated it to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry. And this hadith was narrated from Anas from many channels, and we do not know of anyone narrating it from Mansur except Warqa, nor do we know of anyone narrating it other than Shababab, and we only heard it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, and Mansur did not narrate as musnad other than this hadith."
"7065","7064 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"7066","7065 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"7067","7066 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it. And he did not raise it, and others than Abu Ahmad raised it."
"7068","7067 - Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man drink standing. We said to Qatadah: And eating? He said: Worse, or more filthy. And this hadith was narrated by Shu'bah from Qatadah from Anas, and Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated it from Shu'bah."
"7069","7068 - And with his isnad: that a group of Ukl or Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were people of udders and were not people of countryside, and they found Madinah unhealthy. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered for them some milch camels and a shepherd, and that they go out with them and drink of their urine and their milk. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drove off the camels, and disbelieved after their Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, and they were brought, and he cut their hands and their feet and branded their eyes, and left them in the sun until they died."
"7070","7069 - And Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. And this speech was narrated from Anas from many channels, and we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Shu'bah except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan."
"7071","7070 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"7072","7070 (m) - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, or: woe to you."
"7073","7071 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the front row; if there is a deficiency, it shall be in the last."
"7074","7072 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the first row and the second; if there is a deficiency, it shall be in the third or the fourth. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Anas, nor do we know for it a path from Anas except this path."
"7075","7073 - And Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the rows of men is the first, and the worst of them is the last; and the best of the rows of women is the last, and the worst of them is the first. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this channel, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Sa'id except Abu Asim."
"7076","7074 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, placing his foot upon their sides and slaughtering them with his hand, and saying: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"7077","7075 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned black-and-white rams, and he would mention the name and magnify, and I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
"7078","7076 - Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees in her dream, let her wash. Umm Salamah said, feeling shy of that: Can that be? He said: Yes, so from what is the resemblance? The fluid of the man is thick and white, and the fluid of the woman is thin and yellow; whichever of them rises above, or precedes, the resemblance is from it."
"7079","7077 - Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lay their sides down; of them were those who performed wudu, and of them were those who did not perform wudu."
"7080","7078 - And Ibn Muthanna narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Thabit took suhur. When he finished his suhur, he entered into his prayer. We said to Anas: How much was between his finishing his suhur and his entering into prayer? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"7081","7079 - And with his isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enter into prayer intending to lengthen it, then I hear the crying of the boy, so I shorten my prayer, because of what I know of his mother's anguish at his crying."
"7082","7080 - And with his isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms like the dog."
"7083","7081 - Ibn Muthanna narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you extend his forearms like the dog."
"7084","7082 - And Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in istisqa."
"7085","7083 - Ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Zawra, and a vessel was brought in which was water covering his fingers, or as much as would cover his fingers. He ordered his companions to perform wudu, and placed his palm in the vessel, and we saw the water gushing from between his fingers, until the people performed wudu. We said to Anas: How many were you? He said: Three hundred, or about three hundred."
"7086","7084 - Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pawned a coat of mail of his for a wasq of barley which he took for his family. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Sa'id except Abu Bahr, and Hisham narrated the like of it with other than its wording."
"7087","7085 - Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a man was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they said: He is deceived in buying, so place him under interdiction. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you sell, say: No deceit."
"7088","7086 - And al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this channel with this isnad."
"7089","7087 - Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart of good what weighs an atom."
"7090","7088 - And Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Dirhami narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, and I know it only from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion and no hamah; so who infected the first?"
"7091","7089 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man visiting him, and he was as if a ghost. He said to him: Did you ask your Lord for anything? He said: Yes, I said: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it in the world. He said: Glory be to Allah! Why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in the world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. So the man said it and was cured. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Sa'id except Salim ibn Nuh, and others than Qatadah narrated it; as for from Qatadah, none narrated it except Salim from Sa'id from Qatadah."
"7092","7090 - Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Kathir narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The two tribes, al-Aws and al-Khazraj, boasted. Al-Aws said: Of us is one whose testimony was accepted as the testimony of two men, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit; and of us is one at whose death the Throne shook, Sa'd ibn Mu'adh; and of us is the one washed by the angels, Abdullah ibn Hanzalah; and of us is one whom the wasps protected, Asim ibn Thabit. The Khazrajis said: Of us are four who gathered the Quran, none other gathered it: Ubayy and Mu'adh and Zayd ibn Thabit and Abu Zayd."
"7093","7091 - Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Habbari narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, then took her back. And this hadith, Asbat narrates it from Sa'id from Qatadah as mursal, and he only heard it from Muhammad ibn Thawab from Asbat."
"7094","7092 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in one night. And this hadith is only known from Ma'mar from Qatadah from Anas."
"7095","7093 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Abu Ahmad informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in one night."
"7096","7094 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman followed him, and it shook with them. He said: Be still; a prophet, and a truthful one, and two martyrs. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from the hadith of Qatadah from him, and Sa'id and Imran al-Qattan narrated it from Qatadah."
"7097","7095 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to me, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"7098","7096 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, al-Hajjaj al-Bahili narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"7099","7097 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering, and a Jew passed, and greeted him, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it upon him. He said: Do you know what he said? They said: Yes, he greeted. He said: He said: Death upon you, meaning: you are wished death in your religion; return it upon him. They said: How? He said: Say: Death upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you - meaning: upon you what you said. And this speech, we do not know of anyone narrating it with this wording except Qatadah, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Qatadah except Sa'id."
"7100","7098 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is cupping and Indian costus. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Qatadah from Anas except Sa'id, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Sa'id except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, and Abd al-Wahhab is not strong in hadith, and the people of knowledge accepted his hadith and narrated from him."
"7101","7099 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best? He said: Length of standing. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Anas except from this channel, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Sa'id except Ja'far ibn Awn."
"7102","7100 - Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out with them both together, meaning Hajj and Umrah."
"7103","7101 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together."
"7104","7102 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Ashkib narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise last night and saw in it a palace. I said: Whose is this palace? For a youth of Quraysh? I hoped I would be him, and there it was Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"7105","7103 - And Abd al-Quddus ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated it to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, and he added in it: And I saw slave-girls, or: I saw in it slave-girls, and nothing kept me from entering it except what I know of your jealousy. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah except Ali ibn Asim."
"7106","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Malik al-Susi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Shuba except by the narration of Muhammad ibn Sawa and Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata."
"7107","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month in prayer, supplicating against these tribes: Ril, Dhakwan, Usayya and Banu Lihyan. He said: And Anas informed me that they recited concerning them as Quran: Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and has pleased us."
"7108","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and prostration, for I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"7109","Abda ibn Abd Allah and Said ibn Bahr narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Anas except from this route with this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Said except Muhammad ibn Bishr."
"7110","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Said and Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of completing the prayer."
"7111","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of completing the prayer."
"7112","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said narrated to us, that he was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, so he narrated to us from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it in the last ten, on the ninth, the seventh and the fifth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Said, nor from Said except Abd al-Wahhab."
"7113","One of our companions narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khaybar on half shares. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Said, nor did anyone narrate it from Said except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata."
"7114","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yahya ibn Abi Qurra narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba and Umar ibn Amir narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and wore it on his left, and it is as if I am looking at its glitter on his hand. And this hadith, we do not recall it with this wording from Qatada except from this route, though it has been narrated from Said, from Qatada, from Anas with other than this wording."
"7115","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, who said: Abu al-Mundhir Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought the Buraq, it proved difficult for him, so Jibril, peace be upon him, said: No one more honored to Allah, the Blessed, than him has ever ridden you, so it poured with sweat. And this hadith is only narrated by Said, from Qatada, from Anas, from Malik ibn Sasaah, while Ismail ibn Umar has it abridged."
"7116","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Ubayda al-Haddad Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated to us, from Said, meaning Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for it what He does not give for harshness. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Said other than Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil."
"7117","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear the ring on his right. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada, from Anas, except Said, nor from Said except Abbad."
"7118","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Dhu al-Hulayfa and ordered that it be marked, meaning the sacrificial camels. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except from this route; it is only narrated from Qatada, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas."
"7119","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Umar ibn Said al-Abahh narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: I never touched silk, nor khazz, nor anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7120","And Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated it to us, Musa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through a road of the roads of Madina, they found from him the scent of perfume and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through this road. And this hadith was also narrated by Muadh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was recognized by the scent of perfume."
"7121","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has more right to the house. And this hadith is only narrated from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, while Isa ibn Yunus combined both hadiths together, from Qatada, from Anas, and from al-Hasan, from Samura."
"7122","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said al-Abahh narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate upon a khiwan, nor ate in a sukkurraja, until he met Allah. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Said except by the narration of Umar ibn Said and Abd al-Warith, while Yusuf al-Iskaf narrated it from Qatada, from Anas."
"7123","Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Yunus, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate upon a khiwan, nor ate in a sukkurraja, nor was thin bread baked for him. He said: I said: Then upon what did they eat? He said: Upon leather mats."
"7124","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years; he never said for something I did: Why did you do it? Nor for something I did not do: Why did you not do it?"
"7125","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The servant will be married in Paradise to seventy wives. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, can he bear them? He said: He will be given the strength of a hundred."
"7126","Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we recognized it in his face."
"7127","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should spit in front of him in his prayer, but to his left or under his foot."
"7128","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Said, meaning Ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"7129","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Ghusn narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah break the fast for Maghrib while fasting until he broke it even with a drink of water. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from this route with this chain, while al-Qasim ibn al-Ghusn is not strong in hadith; only what is not preserved from others is written from his hadith."
"7130","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The People of the Book greet us, so how do we reply to them? He said: Say: And upon you. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abi Aruba with other than this wording, so we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"7131","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, says: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; when he draws near a cubit, I draw near an armspan; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening. And the meaning of this hadith: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan in obedience, I draw near to him a cubit in acceptance; when he draws near a cubit, I draw near an armspan; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening, meaning: I accept it from him."
"7132","And with its chain, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and I do not know whether something was revealed or he used to say it: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would wish, or seek, a second, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"7133","And Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it to us, Umayya ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ali ibn Masaada narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, with similar wording."
"7134","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas, who said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which no one after me will narrate to you having heard it from him? Among the signs of the Hour: knowledge will be lifted, ignorance will appear, adultery will spread, wine will be drunk, men will go and women will remain, until there is for fifty women one caretaker."
"7135","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Qatada, from Anas, so we sufficed with those we named."
"7136","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy ibn Kab: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to recite to you: Those who disbelieved. He said: Did He name me?! He said: Yes. He said: So Ubayy wept. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Anas, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Anas except Qatada. And more than one narrated it from Qatada, the most eminent who narrated it from him being Shuba."
"7137","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner garment and my receptacle; people will increase and they will decrease, so accept from their doers of good and pardon their doers of wrong."
"7138","And with its chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have supplicated to Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave."
"7139","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two."
"7140","And with its chain, he said: There was a fright in Madina, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse called Mandub, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have seen no fright, and we found him to be a sea. And this hadith we already mentioned from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas with other than this wording, so we repeated it from Shuba since the wording of the hadith of Shuba differs from the wording of the hadith of Said."
"7141","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None believes until I am more beloved to him than his child and all people."
"7142","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, whoever has them finds the taste of faith: one who loves a person loving him only for Allah; one to whom Allah and His Messenger are more beloved than anything besides them; and one to whom being cast into the Fire is more beloved than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas from a better route than this route, nor more authentic."
"7143","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said: Is there among you anyone from other than you? They said: No, except a sisters son of ours. He said: The sisters son of a people is of them. Then he said: Are you not pleased that they return with the world while you return with the Messenger of Allah to your houses? If people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"7144","And with its chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, life is the life of the Hereafter, or he said: There is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive, or honor, the Ansar and the Muhajira."
"7145","And with its chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and it was said to him: It was given in charity to Barira. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"7146","And with its chain, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, and I did not hear any of them recite: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"7147","And with its chain, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved pumpkin, so food was brought to him, or he was invited to it. Anas said: So I kept following it and placing it before him, for I knew he loved it."
"7148","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet but that he warned his nation of the one-eyed liar; indeed he is one-eyed, while your Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is: disbeliever."
"7149","And with its chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion, no omens, and good omens please me. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: The good word."
"7150","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion and no omens, and good omens please me. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: The good word."
"7151","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, cursing Ril and Dhakwan."
"7152","And Muhammad narrated it to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, supplicating against a tribe of the Arabs, then left it."
"7153","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of the people of Paradise who would like to return to the world except the martyr, for he loves to return to the world and says: Until I am killed ten times, for what he sees of what Allah has given him of honor."
"7154","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Qatada informed us, who said: I heard Anas saying: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have prepared nothing for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are with whom you love. And I never saw the Muslims rejoice at anything after Islam more intensely than their rejoicing at his saying."
"7155","And with its chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The son of Adam grows old, while two remain of him: greed and hope."
"7156","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"7157","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, who said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk wine, so he lashed him with two palm stalks about forty times; Abu Bakr did the same; then when Umar came he consulted the people, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: The lightest of the prescribed punishments is eighty, so Umar ordered it."
"7158","And with it, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, while in his heart is good weighing an atom; and bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, while in his heart is good weighing a grain of wheat; and I do not know with which of them he began."
"7159","And with it, he said: I heard Qatada narrating from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the Romans, they said: They do not read a letter unless sealed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, it is as if I am looking at its whiteness on the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its engraving: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"7160","And with it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for establishing the row is part of completing the prayer."
"7161","And with it, he said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7162","Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"7163","And with it, he said: I asked Anas about the nabidh of jars, and he said: I did not hear anything about it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though he used to dislike it."
"7164","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada and Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mix with us, or treat us kindly, such that he would say to a small brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do? And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, except Said ibn Amir."
"7165","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada and Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to treat us kindly, such that he would say to a small brother of mine: Abu Umayr, what did the nughayr do?"
"7166","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that a people testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the sighting of the crescent, the crescent of Shawwal, so he ordered them to break the fast and to go out to their Eid. And in this hadith Said ibn Amir made an error; Shuba only narrated it from Abu Bishr, from Abu Umayr ibn Anas: that uncles of his testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7167","Amr ibn Isa narrated to us, Abu Bahr narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Lord, the Blessed and Exalted."
"7168","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a garment of sundus, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marveled at it, so he said: Do you marvel at this? By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise are better than it."
"7169","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Ashath ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hell keeps saying: Are you filled, and saying: Is there more, until the Compeller, the Blessed and Exalted, places His Foot in it, and it says: Enough, enough."
"7170","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Hell keeps saying: Is there more, until Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, places His Foot, and it says: Enough, enough; while there remains space in Paradise until Allah creates a creation and settles them in the extra space of Paradise. It is stopped; thus said al-Taymi."
"7171","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anbari narrated to us, Harami ibn Umara narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba except Harami ibn Umara."
"7172","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is a supplication with which he supplicated for his nation, and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba except Rawh ibn Ubada."
"7173","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"7174","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your little servant, so supplicate to Allah for him. And he mentioned the hadith."
"7175","Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada and Musa ibn Anas, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, except Yahya ibn Said; Shuba only narrates it from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, but Yahya ibn Said combined Qatada and Musa. Abu Masud erred and narrated it from Abu Dawud, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, while with Abu Dawud it is: from Shuba, from Musa ibn Anas, and from Hammam, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7176","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, he said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"7177","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Complete the bowing and prostration, for by Allah I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate."
"7178","And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left or under his foot."
"7179","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I was giving Abu Talha and Suhayl ibn Bayda drink from a waterskin containing a mixture of unripe and ripe dates, when someone entered upon us and said: Something new happened today. We said: What is it? He said: Wine has been forbidden. He said: So we poured it out."
"7180","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The most beloved garment for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to wear was the hibara. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Qatada other than Hisham."
"7181","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date and said: Were it not that it might be charity, I would have eaten it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada except Hisham and Hammad ibn Salama, while Talha ibn Musarrif narrated it from Anas."
"7182","And with it: that two men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark night, with them something like two lamps lighting before them; then when they parted, one remained with each of them, until he reached his family. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada other than Hisham."
"7183","And with it, from Anas: that he walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with barley bread and rancid melted fat, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mortgaged a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madina and taken barley from him for his family; and I heard him three times saying: There never remained with the family of Muhammad a sa of wheat nor a sa of dates, while he had on that day nine wives."
"7184","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life and death."
"7185","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we recognized it in his face. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. And this hadith, we did not hear anyone narrating it from Muadh except Muhammad ibn Umar, and he was trustworthy; this hadith is only known from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Utba, from Abu Said al-Khudri, while Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated it from Said, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Abu Said."
"7186","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram at the end of a prayer. And this hadith, we did not hear it from anyone narrating it from Muadh except Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, who is the son-in-law of Muadh ibn Hisham; this hadith is only narrated from Qatada, from Abu Hassan, from Ibn Abbas."
"7187","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hammad ibn Masada narrated to us, from Qurra, from Qatada, from Anas. [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"7188","And Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father informed us, from Qurra, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uhud: A mountain that loves us and we love it."
"7189","Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Qurra narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, he said: When we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"7190","Abu Kamil and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who plants a crop or plants a seedling, then a human, bird or beast eats from it, except it is charity for him."
"7191","Abu Kamil and Hilal ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: People after Ismail were upon Islam, then Satan would whisper things to people, wanting to turn them away from Islam, until he introduced to them in the talbiya: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service; at Your service, You have no partner, except a partner that is Yours, You own him and what he owns. He said: It continued until he took them out of Islam into polytheism."
"7192","Hilal ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that three men of those before you among people went out one day seeking pasture for their families, when rain seized them, so they entered a cave, and a protruding rock fell upon them, of which they saw no opening. So some of them said to others: The rock has fallen and the trace is effaced, and none knows your place except Allah, so supplicate to Allah by your most firmly established deeds. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel, then come to them, and when I found them sleeping, I would stand over their heads until they woke. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved. The other said: O Allah, if You know that a woman pleased me, and I set a reward for her, then when I overcame her, I handed her reward to her, while she fled with herself. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So two thirds of the rock moved. And the other said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a laborer for work he would do, then he came to me seeking his wage, while I was angry, so I turned him away; he went and left his wage. So I took that wage of his, gathered it and invested it, until all wealth came from it. O Allah, if You know I only did that hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So the rock moved, and they walked out. And these three hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Abu Awana, from Qatada, from Anas."
"7193","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"7194","And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"7195","And with it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old, while two of him grow young: greed for wealth and greed for life."
"7196","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, while Allah turns to whoever turns."
"7197","And that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyya and married her, making her freeing her dowry."
"7198","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take sahur, for in sahur there is blessing."
"7199","Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us in a sermon but said in his sermon: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Anas, nor do we know for it a route from Anas except this route; Abu Hilal was narrated from by a group of scholars who accepted his hadith, though he was not a memorizer."
"7200","Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, increase us. He said: And like that. So Umar said: O Abu Bakr, if Allah wills, He will admit them all into Paradise with one handful. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who followed Abu Hilal in his narration; Qatada only narrates it from other than Anas."
